{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/333352-3e-abyssals-exalted-hauntings","id":333352,"title":"3e Abyssals: Exalted Hauntings","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Abyssal Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-12-07T14:02:13-08:00","id":333352,"title":"3e Abyssals: Exalted Hauntings","content":"Here's what I'd really like for third edition Abyssals:<br /> <br /> Deathlords cannot directly influence the exaltation process to choose hosts for <b>every</b> exaltation. This has always been an extremely limiting setting point which ties abyssal motivations directly to the whims of narrowly-focused entities and has NOT been productive for expanding the range of Abyssal character concepts.<br /> <br /> Treat Abyssal exaltation more like a powerful, horrifying alternative to lingering undeath as a ghost. When a mortal dies with unfinished business they might come back as a ghost under their own power or, if their motivation is sufficiently epic enough to impress a corrupted solar exaltation, they might be granted a new lease on life and powers unimaginable so as to fulfill their unfinished purpose. Once that purpose is fulfilled though the contract ends and the exaltation abandons its host-soul to the waters of lethe, or hurls them into oblivion if their goal becomes impossible to achieve.<br /> <br /> Resonance in this case does not come from the Deathlords or the Neverborn but rather from the exaltation itself as punishment to those souls who try and forestall their death by putting off the business the exaltation reanimated them to conclude. Eventually they MUST achieve their goal and in achieving it die finally and permanently. The core principle of destruction is achieved by turning inward, towards the abyssal's own inevitable demise and their struggle between the desire to preserve their life and to achieve their goals.<br /> <br /> I think that about covers it. I'd like opinions if possible. Who would play this? Who sees problems with it? Criticisms welcome especially if you feel I'm missing the point of this splat.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1318,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1318-kindledradial","user":"kindledRadial","date":". 12-07-2014, 05:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1318-kindledradial","name":"kindledRadial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1318_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-07T14:14:43-08:00","id":333386,"title":"","content":"I kind of like the idea of Monstrances - they're like coffins for classic vampires but also kind of function like the cabinet in Lytek's office. I also like the idea of them being optional - of there being free-roaming Black Exaltations that Deathlords lost track or control of. So I'd be good either way, to be honest.<br /> <br /> I like the idea of an Abyssal being suspended forever at the moment of death, forever preserved like the Neverborn between being and non-being (more or less).<br /> <br /> 2E Abyssals states that Resonance comes from the Void itself and the Neverborn are merely channels for its power, so it's already technically disconnected from both the Deathlords and the Neverborn (despite the descriptions of it holding that it results from the anger of the Neverborn). The book plainly states that Resonance is an incurable, innate part of the Black Exaltation itself - it can't be an Abyssal Exaltation without Resonance by its very nature.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"right\"><span style=\"font-size:28px\"><b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">\u263e</span></span></b></span></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/438-wulf","name":"wulf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar438_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-07T14:36:03-08:00","id":333433,"title":"","content":"My complaint about 2e abyssals is that ALL of them are tied to monstrances and thus freely manipulated/tortured/killed by E10 Solar-Abyssal hybrids with no conscience and no real need to retain their servants' free will. This is in and of itself an interesting idea that I want kept, but saying that it is true of the entire splat is limiting. So to clarify, I would want both to be valid character choices.<br /> <br /> Resonance IS an innate feature of the abyssal exaltation but as was commented in I believe Shards of the Exalted Dream, which gave alternative resonance rules which were less &quot;kill everything,&quot; the Neverborn have direct control over it in 2e canon when acting through an abyssal's monstrance. This means that all abyssals with a monstrance (which again, are all abyssals in 2e canon) are JUST as much slaves to the neverborn as they are to whatever truer or baser concepts are represented by the &quot;dark fate.&quot; Again, not a thing I want unwritten, but definitely something I would like a workable alternative to in game.<br /> <br /> I don't think the two ideas are mutually exclusive. Maybe the Deathlords botched the operation to seal away all the Abyssal exaltations and are scrambling to collect them all. Maybe some abyssals willingly submit to Deathlords and the neverborn as a way to prolong their lives and put off their inevitable demise after achieving their goals. Maybe some of them just want soul steel pantaloons and they signed the dotted line in blood and now they have buyer's remorse. Point is, I want more, not less.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1318-kindledradial","name":"kindledRadial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1318_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-07T14:43:59-08:00","id":333438,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wulf</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/333352-3e-abyssals-exalted-hauntings?p=333386#post333386\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I kind of like the idea of Monstrances - they're like coffins for classic vampires but also kind of function like the cabinet in Lytek's office. I also like the idea of them being optional - of there being free-roaming Black Exaltations that Deathlords lost track or control of. So I'd be good either way, to be honest.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Essentially this. An Abyssal Exaltation's distribution can be controlled through the Monstrance if it has one, and the Monstrance is what corrupts the Exaltation into an Abyssal one. The thing to remember is that an Abyssal Exaltation on it's own has the same vague criteria/drive as regular Solar Exaltations, but they can only Exalt people on the verge of death, and their power is Abyssal rather than Solar.<br /> <br /> This means that the Abyssal can be just as much a hero and a Solar, but their brand of heroism is in a dark romantic sense, very Gothic rather than Pulp.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/393-godjaw","name":"Godjaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar393_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"665"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-07T14:45:32-08:00","id":333439,"title":"","content":"I agree, more options are always better than less and I have full confidence that Ex3 will give this to us with more varied and interesting Deathlords, fewer fully-enslaved Deathknights and are more populous and interesting Underworld. Personally, I'd love to see their Blight Effects invested back into their Charmset rather than being kept in Resonance because I love these effects and think they'd be great if they could be generated <i>on purpose</i> and not only because Oblivion is upset with you. I like that Deathknights can reply to their name if its spoken by their Lunar mate, just to throw that out there, and I like that Ex3 will be changing/expanding on what this kind of bond is and how it comes into play.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"right\"><span style=\"font-size:28px\"><b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">\u263e</span></span></b></span></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/438-wulf","name":"wulf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar438_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-07T16:42:50-08:00","id":333563,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Godjaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/333352-3e-abyssals-exalted-hauntings?p=333438#post333438\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> An Abyssal Exaltation's distribution can be controlled through the Monstrance if it has one, and the Monstrance is what corrupts the Exaltation into an Abyssal one. The thing to remember is that an Abyssal Exaltation on it's own has the same vague criteria/drive as regular Solar Exaltations, but they can only Exalt people on the verge of death, and their power is Abyssal rather than Solar.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Sounds like we're all in agreement about keeping the deathlords and monstrances as a setting point, at least. I'd like to say also that this notion that an abyssal exaltation has the same criteria as a solar exaltation is <i>very much</i> my intention here, but that while making them exalt at the time of death is a good start, it's not a final solution for making them distinct in my opinion. After all, most Dawns would probably have died if not for their exaltation's timing, so the distinction between a Dusk and Dawn would be one of only a moment's timing, really.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wulf</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> ...I have full confidence that Ex3 will give this to us with more varied and interesting Deathlords, fewer fully-enslaved Deathknights and are more populous and interesting Underworld.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I am going to disagree here, only because while I do agree that Onyx Path is putting considerable thought and energy into the Underworld setting and I DO appreciate that, it's not the same as actually unbinding abyssal character concepts from the Deathlord narrative. In fact much of what I hear is making me feel that it might be <i>worse</i> in Ex3. They are talking about &quot;Deathlord-based charmsets,&quot; for god's sake. I do <i>not</i> want infernals in the underworld bound to underworld yozi, I want something new and distinct.<br /> <br /> Consider: what if the dev's unveiled their new plan for Lunars in Ex3 and their entire charmset was based around mimicking their Solar mate. Would players consider that extra freedom of thought, because Solars can mean and do so much? Or would that be massively disappointing? To me, it would very much be the latter.<br /> <br /> Perhaps I am trying too hard to reinvent the wheel here, but I really think that there <i>should be</i> something in Ex3 concretely saying that not all abyssals are loyalists, and giving a <i>reasonable</i> justification for that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1318,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1318-kindledradial","user":"kindledRadial","date":". 12-07-2014, 07:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1318-kindledradial","name":"kindledRadial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1318_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-07T17:02:04-08:00","id":333572,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>kindledRadial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/333352-3e-abyssals-exalted-hauntings#post333352\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">directly to the whims of narrowly-focused entities and has NOT been productive for expanding the range of Abyssal character concepts.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think I see the logic here. If you have an Abyssal PC, it can be as broad as any Solar, just that a Deathward thought to notice them and think they might be useful in some way to their goals.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>kindledRadial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/333352-3e-abyssals-exalted-hauntings#post333352\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Resonance in this case does not come from the Deathlords or the Neverborn but rather from the exaltation itself as punishment to those souls who try and forestall their death by putting off the business the exaltation reanimated them to conclude. Eventually they MUST achieve their goal and in achieving it die finally and permanently..</div> </div> </div> </div>I cannot get behind this; it is fairly antithetical to the notion of Exaltation at all.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>kindledRadial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/333352-3e-abyssals-exalted-hauntings?p=333433#post333433\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My complaint about 2e abyssals is that ALL of them are tied to monstrances and thus freely manipulated/tortured/killed by E10 Solar-Abyssal hybrids with no conscience and no real need to retain their servants' free will.</div> </div> </div> </div>The solution here is fixing the Deathlords and their relationship with Abyssals. Having a major plot point being the 13 Ghosts of Scooby-Doo who all want to kill the world is boring and redundant, it's good that the authors have realized this.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-07T17:27:08-08:00","id":333581,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>kindledRadial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/333352-3e-abyssals-exalted-hauntings?p=333563#post333563\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In fact much of what I hear is making me feel that it might be <i>worse</i> in Ex3. They are talking about &quot;Deathlord-based charmsets,&quot; for god's sake. I do <i>not</i> want infernals in the underworld bound to underworld yozi, I want something new and distinct.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Ah see, there's your confusion. The charms are informed by the Deathlords like Solar charms are informed by the UCS. They aren't actually their charms, but thematically stylized and informed by their natures and powers. For example in the Abyssal Preview, there were charms that summoned phantasmal armor around you, or infused Soulsteel armor with haunting faces that moan and bite at enemy weapons, call spectral chains of pyreflame to act as additional limbs, and summon forth an iron maiden of armor around a foe, who if killed by it could be reanimated under the Abyssals control, encased in the damned armor. Does this at all sound familiar? It's because they're themed after the First and Forsaken Lion. Nothing about how he teaches these things, or Abyssals are using his power, merely thematically informed which gives both really cool powers for the Abyssals, and characterizes the Deathlords without them even needing to be actual characters if need be.<br /> <br /> Wanting new and distinct is great, and these charms informed by the Deathlords are awesome, but Abyssals are also the dark mirror of Solars, so many powers will be dark mirrors but in meaningful ways, not just a mirror keyword.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":393,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/393-godjaw","user":"Godjaw","date":". 12-07-2014, 08:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/393-godjaw","name":"Godjaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar393_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"665"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-07T17:29:42-08:00","id":333582,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/333352-3e-abyssals-exalted-hauntings?p=333572#post333572\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think I see the logic here. If you have an Abyssal PC, it can be as broad as any Solar, just that a Deathward thought to notice them and think they might be useful in some way to their goals.</div> </div> </div> </div>The logic is that if I have a cool character concept I never want my storyteller to tell me &quot;you can't do that, Sam the Overlord wouldn't like that.&quot; and for that to be reasonable grounds upon which to scrap the character. I don't want to tailor MY player experience to an NPC. That sucks. If I want to make an abyssal cake-froster I want my storyteller to say something like &quot;that's not really on theme for an abyssal, maybe try Ex3 Lunars instead. They have an entire charmset for that.&quot; In Ex2 deathlords were like this giant STOP sign in front of any abyssal character concept that didn't want to unravel the very fabric of creation eventually and I want that to stop.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/333352-3e-abyssals-exalted-hauntings?p=333572#post333572\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I cannot get behind this; it is fairly antithetical to the notion of Exaltation at all.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm gonna need you to explain your problem a bit more if you want a response. Which part is antithetical? And antithetical to ALL exalted or just Abyssals?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/333352-3e-abyssals-exalted-hauntings?p=333572#post333572\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The solution here is fixing the Deathlords and their relationship with Abyssals. Having a major plot point being the 13 Ghosts of Scooby-Doo who all want to kill the world is boring and redundant, it's good that the authors have realized this.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's what we're discussing. A fix for the deathlord's relationship with abyssals. Currently they have absolute control over <i>all </i>abyssal exaltations. That's the part I want changed. What do <i>you </i>see as the problem there?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1318-kindledradial","name":"kindledRadial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1318_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-07T17:29:58-08:00","id":333583,"title":"","content":"I like that the new Abyssal Charms are Deathlord-flavoured for a few reasons: It makes the Abyssal Charmset more distinct from the Solar Charmset and it forces the writers to make the Deathlords that much more interesting if they'll be the inspiration for entire Charmsets.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"right\"><span style=\"font-size:28px\"><b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">\u263e</span></span></b></span></div>","edited":{"userid":438,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/438-wulf","user":"wulf","date":". 12-07-2014, 08:43 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/438-wulf","name":"wulf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar438_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-07T17:34:11-08:00","id":333586,"title":"","content":"Wulf: Yes and yes. I'm a bit worried they <i>might</i> decide to base their <i>entire</i> charmset around the Deathlords though, which really is nothing distinct from infernals. Abyssals never stood apart in Ex2 and I feel like there's enough substance there that they can aim higher than just copying another splat. Not opposed to the Deathlords opening their charmset to loyalists, though, and for that being a major draw for deathknight recruitment.<br /> <br /> General: I'm always happy to spark a debate about changing the Deathlord canon so this thread is gold to me, but to draw back to the original post I wanted to brainstorm an idea of what deathknights look like <i>without</i> the deathlords and neverborn controlling them, since we didn't get much player support for that in Ex2. The alternative resonance rules in Shards were just about the only helping hand on that note in fact. Hell, even the Infernals got the Devil Tiger charms as a potential out and eternal servitude actually makes <i>sense</i> for them, somewhat.<br /> <br /> I like the idea of abyssals being like vengeful spirits because ghosts are fascinating to me but they are constantly ignored in Exalted because of their low power tier. I think making Abyssals work like super-ghosts could make players and character both care a lot more about the undead in general, as opposed to just ignoring the underworld which is kinda what they do in canon until a shadowland is within 50 miles.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1318,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1318-kindledradial","user":"kindledRadial","date":". 12-07-2014, 08:46 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1318-kindledradial","name":"kindledRadial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1318_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-07T17:58:44-08:00","id":333623,"title":"","content":"Got to admit I dislike this idea, largely because I'm one of the few that am perfectly comfortable with slavery being art and parcel of BEING a death knight","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-07T18:04:20-08:00","id":333629,"title":"","content":"PoN: But you understand that within this setting you could still do that character concept, right? What is it about making it true of <i>all</i> abyssals that you like?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1318-kindledradial","name":"kindledRadial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1318_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-07T18:24:42-08:00","id":333642,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>kindledRadial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/333352-3e-abyssals-exalted-hauntings?p=333582#post333582\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The logic is that if I have a cool character concept I never want my storyteller to tell me &quot;you can't do that, Sam the Overlord wouldn't like that&quot; and for that to be reasonable grounds upon which to scrap the character. I don't want to tailor MY player experience to an NPC. That sucks. If I want to make an abyssal cake-froster I want my storyteller to say something like &quot;that's not really on theme for an abyssal, maybe try Ex3 Lunars instead. They have an entire charmset for that.&quot; In Ex2 deathlords were like this giant STOP sign in front of any abyssal character concept that didn't want to unravel the very fabric of creation eventually and I want that to stop.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's a shitty/controlling ST problem, not a setting problem. Changing setting ideas will not change that problem.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>kindledRadial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/333352-3e-abyssals-exalted-hauntings?p=333582#post333582\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm gonna need you to explain your problem a bit more if you want a response. Which part is antithetical? And antithetical to ALL exalted or just Abyssals?</div> </div> </div> </div>I cannot get behind the notion that the Exaltation itself is going to punish those bearing its power, for using its power. This was tried with Paradox and 2e Resonance. Both were utter shit.<br /> <br /> &quot;Resonance in this case does not come from the Deathlords or the Neverborn but rather from the exaltation itself as punishment to those souls who try and forestall their death by putting off the business the exaltation reanimated them to conclude. Eventually they MUST achieve their goal and in achieving it die finally and permanently.&quot; The notion that your own power punishes you, and ultimately kills you, for wielding it as you choose is not something I would ever want to see in print. I find that to be antithetical to the nature of Exaltation as an uplifting miracle, even if that uplifting is not always a nice or positive thing. The uplifting power is amoral and sustains you, not destroys you.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>kindledRadial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/333352-3e-abyssals-exalted-hauntings?p=333582#post333582\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's what we're discussing. A fix for the deathlord's relationship with abyssals. Currently they have absolute control over <i>all </i>abyssal exaltations. That's the part I want changed. What do <i>you </i>see as the problem there?</div> </div> </div> </div>The shitty boring portrayal of the Deathlords, period. This is already known to not be carried forward. I am fine with the &quot;absolute&quot; control over who gets to Exalt as an Abyssal. My problem is how the Deathlords themselves in 2e were both boring cliche characters and also had broken, terrible, lazy mechanics, neither of which I am particularly worried about in the future.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":3420,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","user":"Zelbinnean","date":". 12-07-2014, 09:26 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-07T19:29:16-08:00","id":333682,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>kindledRadial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/333352-3e-abyssals-exalted-hauntings?p=333586#post333586\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wulf: Yes and yes. I'm a bit worried they <i>might</i> decide to base their <i>entire</i> charmset around the Deathlords though, which really is nothing distinct from infernals. Abyssals never stood apart in Ex2 and I feel like there's enough substance there that they can aim higher than just copying another splat. Not opposed to the Deathlords opening their charmset to loyalists, though, and for that being a major draw for deathknight recruitment.</div> </div> </div> </div> Ok ignoring the fact that at my last information the infernals are not just drawing their powers from Yozi in the third, so that's a thing. You seem to be misinterpreting how this is going to work, from what we've heard, by assuming they'll just copy infernals. As Wulf said the abyssal charms are set to be informed by a deathlord, but that's it. You want an abyssal who's able to wrap people around them with their charms then The Lover is probably one of if not the best study source for learning how to do it. This isn't a case &quot;The power of Malfeas flows through me as a result I can channel the power Ligier to immolate my foes.&quot; It's more of &quot;I watched the Heart of Malfeas grab a screaming foe by its throat and as emerald fire poured from his grip to devour the doomed soul I decided that I too would wield this power.&quot; That and something else I read indicated that abyssals will probably start some charm trees the same way as a solar will because there isn't much that changes between the theme of hero, death, and monster (or whatever an infernal is going to be) when the power is creating a sword from your own energy. Then it moves off on the themes.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>kindledRadial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/333352-3e-abyssals-exalted-hauntings?p=333586#post333586\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I like the idea of abyssals being like vengeful spirits because ghosts are fascinating to me but they are constantly ignored in Exalted because of their low power tier. I think making Abyssals work like super-ghosts could make players and character both care a lot more about the undead in general, as opposed to just ignoring the underworld which is kinda what they do in canon until a shadowland is within 50 miles.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you look at the deathknights and your thought is &quot;They're super-ghosts,&quot; then you see something very different than I do.I saw the Deathlords as super-ghosts, but the deathknights never struck me as ghosts. They were things that cheated death an option was presented to them and they lept for the chance to not fall into their grave. To use an explanation I once told a player among the undead I would say Abyssals are almost Kryptonian Vampires. <br /> <br /> As for ignoring the underworld, well what did you expect if you're a nonabyssal then you have no power there; there is nothing of any real value there; and you have enough problems dealing with the world of the living, and its incursions from hell and the never-should as well as the idiocy the living get up to to, to bother dealing with people who should already have moved on with their finished lives and moved on to new potentially horrible lives.<br /> <br /> Also I'm with Zelb that idea on resonance being because you're exaltation is punishing you for accepting and forcing you to finish up and die is horrible.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-08T11:59:32-08:00","id":334401,"title":"","content":"I see a lot of the same comments so I'm going to post here in general and I apologize if your specific comments are not addressed.<br /> <br /> 1: Abyssals are not Solars. They have and deserve themes beyond the Solar narrative of &quot;infinite cosmic power and indefatigable pursuit of mastery.&quot; This is not a bad theme. Solars do this well, people love it, it's written well, it is NOT what every exalted story is about. Being an exalt should make you feel like a badass, yes, but that should not be the sum total of your experience as an Abyssal, as a Lunar, as an Infernal. These should be different stories. Abyssal narratives are very much the<b> <u>tragic</u></b> hero narrative, where not every attempt to do good is thwarted but every step forward comes at a known price. Perhaps my idea is not the best way to represent this, if people have ideas on how to improve it then I'd love to hear it, but Resonance is a great mechanic that is every bit as essential to the Abyssal narrative as Limit Break is to the Solar. An Abyssal without a Dark Fate is not an Abyssal, period.<br /> <br /> 2: There is a <i>lot</i> of valuable stuff in the underworld, both in the sense of epic loot and in the sense of narrative. Ghosts have plenty of story hooks and plot devices to use, a story set in the underworld can be very very engaging. It's just that no one ever pays ghosts any mind because they are &quot;just ghosts&quot; in much the same way that mortals are ignored for being &quot;just humans.&quot; They only become scary after about a thousand years of down time. What I had hoped to bring to the table with my idea was the popular notion in Creation that some people come back as &quot;super-ghosts&quot; that are immediately terrifying to <i>everyone</i>, even the celestial exalted. That fear would make ghosts matter in much the same way that Solar exaltation makes mortals matter. That is the aim.<br /> <br /> (Sidenote: I actually really like the description of Deathlords as Kryptonian vampires. It's oximoronic but so are they sometimes.)<br /> <br /> 3: Deathlords should not be undead Yozi. I don't mean to say that the Yozi are not good charm fodder, they are, but rather that the method and justification for the charmset establishes a theme I dislike being used more than once. It worked very well for Infernals in Ex2 because these were stories about people who had sold their soul to some flavor of &quot;the devil&quot; and paid the price in the form of eternal servitude and forced mutation into something altogether inhuman. This is Faustian, this is scary, this is very very on point for Infernals. This should be an Infernal theme, not an &quot;evil solar&quot; theme. Abyssals can be more than Infernals with soulsteel chasing.<br /> <br /> 4: Adding more flavors to the Deathlords does not solve all the problems that plagued the Abyssals in Ex2. It is something that <i>should</i> <i>be done</i> and I'm glad they are working on it, but it is not a cure-all. The Deathlords serve the Neverborn in their eternal struggle to end all life. Having 36 flavors of &quot;I kill a dude&quot; was not good enough to make Abyssals distinct in Ex2, it won't be enough to make them distinct in Ex3. &quot;Like Solars but more kill-y&quot; is not a good enough splat concept. <i>Everyone</i> kills things in Exalted. Abyssals deserve to be infused with more than that and there is plenty of room to explore new concepts <i>if</i> we are given narrative license to make characters unbound from the Deathlord's ultimate goal of &quot;undo Creation.&quot; Until we get that license Abyssal concepts will always be limited, <i>that</i> is my problem, that is what I want fixed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1318,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1318-kindledradial","user":"kindledRadial","date":". 12-08-2014, 03:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1318-kindledradial","name":"kindledRadial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1318_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-08T13:12:56-08:00","id":334492,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>kindledRadial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/333352-3e-abyssals-exalted-hauntings?p=334401#post334401\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">[snip]</div> </div> </div> </div>1. True, they are not. They are the dark mirrors of Solars, infused with deathly essence and powers. Abyssals can be tragic heroes, they can also be gothic heroes and anti-heroes. As for a Dark Fate. I am firm in my opinion a player should never be punished for using their toys. Things like Limit, and Dark Fate should facilitate storytelling, players should want to break because it's entertaining.<br /> <br /> 2.I agree with this notion of developing ghosts into something interesting, but comparing them to Exalted is not the way it should be done. They should be interesting on their own merits, not how they compare to others.<br /> <br /> 3.I also believe in this idea. Deathlords are masters to the Abyssal apprentice, and this relationship can be redefined. They should not be undoubtedly slaves, but being a slave is an open character concept. I find it much more evocative an Abyssal shard Exalting someone on the precipice of death, without Deathlord intervention, however meeting a Deathlord at the Crossroads and taking their black gift should also be valid.<br /> <br /> 4.Well the ultimate goal of undo-ing Creation is unlikely to be prevalent. They're 13 individuals with individual goals. The Neverborn are being de-emphasized and Oblivion is having some kind of change in it's cosmic significance which we don't know yet.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/393-godjaw","name":"Godjaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar393_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"665"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-08T13:21:44-08:00","id":334499,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rater202</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Add the fact the the relationship between the lords and knights has been confirmed to be &quot;Master and aprentice&quot; rather than &quot;Master and slave&quot; this time around.</div> </div> </div> </div>Or alternatively, &quot;none.&quot; Independent Abyssals were introduced in the tail end of 2e, but they've been much more built into the expectations of their 3e presentation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines.</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/user?u=451515\" target=\"_blank\">Robert Vance's Patreon</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/527-robert-vance","name":"Robert Vance","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar527_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-08T13:28:36-08:00","id":334506,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Vance</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/333352-3e-abyssals-exalted-hauntings?p=334499#post334499\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Or alternatively, &quot;none.&quot; Independent Abyssals were introduced in the tail end of 2e, but they've been much more built into the expectations of their 3e presentation.</div> </div> </div> </div>*Hugs*<br /> <br /> This is the best news since I found out what Liminals are!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1520732-forged-by-purpose-alchemicals-peach\" target=\"_blank\">Forged By Purpose: The Alchemicals</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1413451-dead-but-not-gone-ghosts\" target=\"_blank\">Dead But Not Gone: Ghosts</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/228291-ghosts-a-revision-peach\" target=\"_blank\">Ghosts: A Revision</a> (2nd Edition)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/316-masters-of-the-industrial-elements-2e-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Masters of the Industrial Elements</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1157362-from-the-crucible-crafting-as-a-struggle-peach\" target=\"_blank\">\u200bFrom The Crucible: Crafting As A Struggle</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/74-kyeudo","name":"Kyeudo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar74_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1723"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-08T15:49:05-08:00","id":334610,"title":"","content":"Here's the thing about playing independent abyssals in Ex2: the amount of resources the deathlords can and would muster to pursue a traitorous abyssal would put the Wyld Hunt to shame. The deathlords <i>know</i> that a free abyssal could overpower them if they grew strong enough, they have <i>had</i> solaroid exaltations before so they know what to expect, and if they have your monstrance then they can freely kill you at any time they choose. I agree with Godjaw that it would be fun to allow this angle for players who <i>want</i> to pursue it or to take up the extra challenge, but making it the norm for all is putting a tall, tall hurdle in between you and playing a free abyssal in the setting who is still going to be alive at any time in the near future.<br /> <br /> I think one thing that is missing from this discussion on resonance is that it <i>doesn't</i> punish you for using your powers, it punishes you for using your powers <i>the wrong way</i>. This is the core of the abyssal tragedy: that an external but innate force which cannot be ignored is forcing them to act a certain way, and acting against it <i>will</i> require sacrifices. This does not mean you <i>have</i> to abide by resonance rules, but breaking those rules is part of the drama, the conflict, the pathos of an abyssal exalt. The rules are there and we <i>expect</i> people to break them, that's why they are fun. If you want to talk about actual limitations talk about their charmset, which had fuck all besides murder charms going for it in Ex2.<br /> <br /> And ghosts in Exalted already <i>are</i> interesting. Read the fluff on the lords of Stygia's districts sometime, those are some very well thought out characters. The whole Underworld book is chalk-full of interesting NPCs, and you'd be hard pressed to name even <i>one</i> of them that showed up in a campaign because if they did they'd be hammered into soul steel within seconds. Normal ghosts are not a threat to the exalted. Which means that compared to all the horrifying stuff that <i>is</i> they take a distant backseat in terms of importance. The problem is that the <i>characters</i> also feel this way, which is why there's basically no exchange between the Underworld and other realms besides the Deathlords. They simply don't matter. Until you build ghosts up to be significant somehow, they never will find major purchase in the exalted setting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1318-kindledradial","name":"kindledRadial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1318_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-08T20:56:23-08:00","id":334794,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>kindledRadial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/333352-3e-abyssals-exalted-hauntings?p=334610#post334610\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Here's the thing about playing independent abyssals in Ex2: the amount of resources the deathlords can and would muster to pursue a traitorous abyssal would put the Wyld Hunt to shame. The deathlords <i>know</i> that a free abyssal could overpower them if they grew strong enough, they have <i>had</i> solaroid exaltations before so they know what to expect, and if they have your monstrance then they can freely kill you at any time they choose. I agree with Godjaw that it would be fun to allow this angle for players who <i>want</i> to pursue it or to take up the extra challenge, but making it the norm for all is putting a tall, tall hurdle in between you and playing a free abyssal in the setting who is still going to be alive at any time in the near future.</div> </div> </div> </div>Or the Monstrance won't be as deadly an anchor as it was in 2e and the Deathlords won't each own continent's worth of resources?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I think one thing that is missing from this discussion on resonance is that it <i>doesn't</i> punish you for using your powers, it punishes you for using your powers <i>the wrong way</i>. This is the core of the abyssal tragedy: that an external but innate force which cannot be ignored is forcing them to act a certain way, and acting against it <i>will</i> require sacrifices. This does not mean you <i>have</i> to abide by resonance rules, but breaking those rules is part of the drama, the conflict, the pathos of an abyssal exalt. The rules are there and we <i>expect</i> people to break them, that's why they are fun. If you want to talk about actual limitations talk about their charmset, which had fuck all besides murder charms going for it in Ex2. </div> </div> </div>I think you are missing the point of Exalted. The Exalted don't have jack anything capable of forcing them to do anything short of the Great Curse. They especially are not at odds with their own Exaltation.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And ghosts in Exalted already <i>are</i> interesting. Read the fluff on the lords of Stygia's districts sometime, those are some very well thought out characters. The whole Underworld book is chalk-full of interesting NPCs, and you'd be hard pressed to name even <i>one</i> of them that showed up in a campaign because if they did they'd be hammered into soul steel within seconds. Normal ghosts are not a threat to the exalted. Which means that compared to all the horrifying stuff that <i>is</i> they take a distant backseat in terms of importance. The problem is that the <i>characters</i> also feel this way, which is why there's basically no exchange between the Underworld and other realms besides the Deathlords. They simply don't matter. Until you build ghosts up to be significant somehow, they never will find major purchase in the exalted setting. </div> </div> </div>Sounds like the problem is not to make Abyssals into ghosts, but to make ghosts able to stand on their own. Stop thinking this is 2nd Edition and no one without a perfect defense and a surprise negator can be dangerous or important.<br /> <br /> Besides, fixing ghosts up isn't that hard. I've already done one rework of ghost mechanics and it wasn't that hard. Throw some new fluff trimming down the Deathlord's kingdoms to a more manageable size and making some connections between Underworld and Creation and you have ghosts worthy of respect.<br /> <br /> Reminds me of the one time I used ghosts as a combat encounter. I threw seven ghosts of various experience levels at a team of a Solar, Abyssal, Terrestrial, and Lunar. They ran scared.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1520732-forged-by-purpose-alchemicals-peach\" target=\"_blank\">Forged By Purpose: The Alchemicals</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1413451-dead-but-not-gone-ghosts\" target=\"_blank\">Dead But Not Gone: Ghosts</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/228291-ghosts-a-revision-peach\" target=\"_blank\">Ghosts: A Revision</a> (2nd Edition)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/316-masters-of-the-industrial-elements-2e-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Masters of the Industrial Elements</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1157362-from-the-crucible-crafting-as-a-struggle-peach\" target=\"_blank\">\u200bFrom The Crucible: Crafting As A Struggle</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/74-kyeudo","name":"Kyeudo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar74_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1723"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-08T21:27:59-08:00","id":334817,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>kindledRadial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/333352-3e-abyssals-exalted-hauntings?p=334610#post334610\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think one thing that is missing from this discussion on resonance is that it <i>doesn't</i> punish you for using your powers, it punishes you for using your powers <i>the wrong way</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>Heavy-handed enforcement of a couple peoples' views on what constituted &quot;appropriate&quot; stories for Abyssals to participate in restricted an entire splat to mere handful of plotlines in which your own soul didn't reach up and strangle you for not being eeeeevil enough. That is neither good mechanical design nor a good way to build thematic behavioral incentives: heavy sticks don't work as-intended, they just build resentment between players and the ST.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-08T22:18:40-08:00","id":334832,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Vance</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/333352-3e-abyssals-exalted-hauntings?p=334499#post334499\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Or alternatively, &amp;quot;none.&amp;quot; Independent Abyssals were introduced in the tail end of 2e, but they've been much more built into the expectations of their 3e presentation.</div> </div> </div> </div>Just signing in to say, Wooooo!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://exalted-golden-shackles-iron-crowns.obsidianportal.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://exalted-golden-shackles-iron...dianportal.com</a> Visit Golden Shackles, Iron Crowns; a 3rd Edition Exalted Campaign ongoing since 2014","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2711-janissary87","name":"Janissary87","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2711_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"444"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-08T23:07:20-08:00","id":334866,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyeudo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/333352-3e-abyssals-exalted-hauntings?p=334794#post334794\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Or the Monstrance won't be as deadly an anchor as it was in 2e and the Deathlords won't each own continent's worth of resources?<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>GOD I hope so. Like if we at least get that out of Ex3 then I promise I won't lodge a single complaint else-wise. The Deathlords as written have zero balancing points in canon and they tilt the whole Underworld on that axis until there is no other head space left for storytellers. Other undead entities besides them may as well not exist.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyeudo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/333352-3e-abyssals-exalted-hauntings?p=334794#post334794\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think you are missing the point of Exalted. The Exalted don't have jack anything capable of forcing them to do anything short of the Great Curse. They especially are not at odds with their own Exaltation.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Well, first of all, Resonance <i>isn't</i> anything short of the Great Curse, the Neverborn <i>invented </i> the Great Curse, then they unbound the abyssal exaltations from it to rebind them to the laws of resonance which are much worse in many ways. So even within that sentence I'd say that Resonance is still kosher.<br /> <br /> More importantly though, are you seriously saying that the celestial exalted have nothing to be afraid of in your game? What are you <i>doing</i> every session? There are lots of things that can force the exalted to bend the knee, including <i>other exalted</i>. The only thing that makes Resonance unique in that respect is that it can never be fully conquered, but it's not an auto-fail dangling above the party's heads, it's the recurring Saturday morning villain that you just can't seem to kill no matter what you do. It's instant conflict. It drives stories. It's an excellent plot device and if you can't handle having something that works against you in Exalted then maybe you should just stick to Solars.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyeudo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/333352-3e-abyssals-exalted-hauntings?p=334794#post334794\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Sounds like the problem is not to make Abyssals into ghosts, but to make ghosts able to stand on their own. Stop thinking this is 2nd Edition and no one without a perfect defense and a surprise negator can be dangerous or important.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>True, there are definitely other and more comprehensive ways of helping ghosts become relevant in their own realm. Nerfing the Deathlords would be a <i>huge </i>firststep. But I think that the celestial exaltation, just by itself, the mere <i>existence</i> of such a thing, has done wonders for making mortals relevant in canon. You can't enslave all of humanity without pissing off a few solars, and that's important for balancing the setting. I want ghosts to have something similar, some fearful thing they can become or do that would give <i>any</i> entity pause, just like the dread spectre of Solar exaltation keeps some of the worst adversaries of Creation at bay.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Heavy-handed enforcement of a couple peoples' views on what constituted &quot;appropriate&quot; stories for Abyssals to participate in restricted an entire splat to mere handful of plotlines in which your own soul didn't reach up and strangle you for not being eeeeevil enough. That is neither good mechanical design nor a good way to build thematic behavioral incentives: heavy sticks don't work as-intended, they just build resentment between players and the ST.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>That's not in any way what's happening with Resonance. To explain again: Resonance is a mechanic that enforces the Dark Fate of Abyssal exaltation by requiring <i>sacrifices</i>. There is nothing in Resonance eruption effects that will prevent you from playing a character concept, it just makes several of them much more painful. This is because Abyssals are a splat <i>focused on heroic sacrifice</i>. If you want to play an exalt who gets everything they want free of charge with a side of hookers and blow and no long-term side effects, <i>play a solar.</i> That is what <i>s</i><i>olars</i> get. I play Abyssals, and have for many many years, because they get <i>more</i> than that. Do whatever you want in your own game, but leave my favorite splat well enough alone when you have <i>plenty</i> of alternatives for playing Grand Theft Yeddim already.<br /> <br /> And may I also point out that this <i>IS </i>the case with Deathlords, ironically, so your position on this issue seems backwards to me. Deathlords in Ex2 were a setting <i>restraint</i> on character concept because they had perfect control over the exaltation process for every abyssal. So White Wolf essentially gave the poorly-written NPC veto power over <i>your</i> character concept. If your storyteller never brought this up with you then either they chose to ignore canon in favor of your character, which was probably wise, or you were playing a loyalist anyway and it never came up. There isn't really a third choice there because if you do obey canon in your game then the Deathlords are impossible to ignore when drafting abyssal characters in Ex2, which again, sucks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1318-kindledradial","name":"kindledRadial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1318_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-08T23:56:16-08:00","id":334898,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>kindledRadial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/333352-3e-abyssals-exalted-hauntings?p=334866#post334866\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's not in any way what's happening with Resonance. To explain again: Resonance is a mechanic that enforces the Dark Fate of Abyssal exaltation by requiring <i>sacrifices</i>. There is nothing in Resonance eruption effects that will prevent you from playing a character concept, it just makes several of them much more painful. This is because Abyssals are a splat <i>focused on heroic sacrifice</i>. If you want to play an exalt who gets everything they want free of charge with a side of hookers and blow and no long-term side effects, <i>play a solar.</i> That is what <i>s</i><i>olars</i> get. I play Abyssals, and have for many many years, because they get <i>more</i> than that. Do whatever you want in your own game, but leave my favorite splat well enough alone when you have <i>plenty</i> of alternatives for playing Grand Theft Yeddim already.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure, but... what are you sacrificing it for? A sacrifice has to have a purpose, and in the case of the Abyssals, it sort of feels like &quot;You either are an evil bastard oooooor everything sucks for you.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I made some Martial Arts for 3e, look at them <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/723442-survival-is-fury-the-monster-reborn-ex3\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> and <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/761356-orgiastic-fugitive-style-3e\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/632-while-my-guitar","name":"While My Guitar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar632_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"606"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-09T00:03:44-08:00","id":334900,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>kindledRadial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/333352-3e-abyssals-exalted-hauntings?p=334866#post334866\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And may I also point out that this <i>IS </i>the case with Deathlords, ironically, so your position on this issue seems backwards to me. Deathlords in Ex2 were a setting <i>restraint</i> on character concept because they had perfect control over the exaltation process for every abyssal. So White Wolf essentially gave the poorly-written NPC veto power over <i>your</i> character concept. If your storyteller never brought this up with you then either they chose to ignore canon in favor of your character, which was probably wise, or you were playing a loyalist anyway and it never came up. There isn't really a third choice there because if you do obey canon in your game then the Deathlords are impossible to ignore when drafting abyssal characters in Ex2, which again, sucks.</div> </div> </div> </div>Except the npc wouldn't have veto over your character concept. The Deathlords are all very insane and while they do have themes they tend to work with when making new deathknights this still doesn't mean your character is vetoed because a Deathlord doesn't potentially agree. I'll prephase this with I don't know how the 1st ed Deathlords were so I can't compare with them there. For a simple example The Bishop of the Chalcedony Thurible generally has his Abyssals handled in such a way that they all double as priests. A friend and I were discussing a character with an intense hatred of religion and theology getting made into one of the Bishop's Abyssals. The reasoning is simple the Bishop is convinced he can bring this foolish child around to the proper ,ie the Bishop's, way of thinking and that this would be an obvious sign of how great his teachings are. We then agreed that said Abyssal had reached a point where the goal was either reality dies or the Bishop dies either or but the theology lectures were going to stop if this character had anything to say about it.<br /> <br /> The other issue with your statement is that there are 13 Deathlords and I think 3-5 of them are intentionally left blank in case you don't want your character with any of the normal options or in your case the character concept just seems to go so very against the canon Deathlords that none of them would choose this person.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-09T00:44:07-08:00","id":334911,"title":"","content":"While My Guitar (Gently weeps?): The thing you are sacrificing for is your motivation. This could be anything (except the deathlords have too much influence over your choices here but more on that later) but part and parcel of the Abyssal experience is that success will hinge on what you are willing to sacrifice to attain your goal. How many innocent people have to die? How many of your other intimacies will fall screaming into the madness of the Abyss? An abyssal can do anything a Solar can do but they always have a price tag attached to it, which makes them interesting. Resonance is not actually about &quot;punishing&quot; anyone, it's about enforcing this theme that your character has a choice to make between what they want and what will hurt others.<br /> <br /> Nalak: The Deathlords are varied in many respects but not in this: they would never keep an abyssal they couldn't control. They have no reason to. People die in the millions every day any one of them could make a decent servant. Some of the more experienced deathknights are harder to replace, yes, but that's irrelevant to a starting character. And the Deathlords all have a job to do: end Creation. And <i>they</i> don't have any more choice than <i>you</i> do about that because they are owned part and parcel by the Neverborn. So while one Deathlord might exalt priests and another harlots and another soldiers, when the time comes to get down to business and start razing creation the abyssal that says &quot;no&quot; and stands by it (somehow) is a very very dead Abyssal in canon. It's the same reason people hate the Ex2 Lunar mate dynamics: having an NPC determine your character's actions is awful.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1318-kindledradial","name":"kindledRadial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1318_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-09T08:11:16-08:00","id":335218,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>kindledRadial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/333352-3e-abyssals-exalted-hauntings?p=334866#post334866\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's not in any way what's happening with Resonance.</div> </div> </div> </div>From an OOC perspective, it sure is.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>kindledRadial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/333352-3e-abyssals-exalted-hauntings?p=334866#post334866\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To explain again: Resonance is a mechanic that enforces the Dark Fate of Abyssal exaltation by requiring <i>sacrifices</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not on the OOC level, it isn't. On the OOC level, the Great Curse is supposed to play up things like mythic hubris, exemplified by Herakles being cursed by Hera to kill his family, or Odysseus looking back when told not to. It tries to facilitate these actions being part and parcel of the heroic experience. It doesn't even really close down concepts. Resonance, by contrast, comes across as a thing designed to enforce one of two particular play styles: loyalism (which it does poorly, since why would you want to stay loyal to a thing that mandates severing all your previous intimacies from your life) or redemption (which heavy-stick mechanics do push one towards; however I think this is a real problem since it sets up the judgmental notion that Abyssals who don't seek redemption are Wrong, and that's equally bad if not worse).<br /> <br /> Sure, IC it pushes sacrifice and alienation. But practically how do you think this comes across? It's a stick with no carrot. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>kindledRadial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/333352-3e-abyssals-exalted-hauntings?p=334866#post334866\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There is nothing in Resonance eruption effects that will prevent you from playing a character concept, it just makes several of them much more painful.</div> </div> </div> </div>There is a difference between &quot;playing a character concept&quot; and &quot;being able to take certain actions that would further the goals of the Neverborn, except the Neverborn punish me for trying to fulfill their goals in that manner/through that route.&quot; The latter is what Resonance effectively does and this is flatly stupid.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>kindledRadial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/333352-3e-abyssals-exalted-hauntings?p=334866#post334866\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is because Abyssals are a splat <i>focused on heroic sacrifice</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't agree. Abyssals are a splat focused on the Faustian deal. The most unfortunate part of this is that, years later, Infernals <i>also </i>became a splat focused on the Faustian deal, except their deal was much sweeter, their lash had fewer barbs, and their leash was much easier to shrug off. Resonance was disliked before Infernals but where compared to Torment, Resonance is clearly a choke chain and that is not really in sync with the notion of playing Exalted.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>kindledRadial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/333352-3e-abyssals-exalted-hauntings?p=334866#post334866\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you want to play an exalt who gets everything they want free of charge with a side of hookers and blow and no long-term side effects, <i>play a solar.</i> That is what <i>s</i><i>olars</i> get. I play Abyssals, and have for many many years, because they get <i>more</i> than that. Do whatever you want in your own game, but leave my favorite splat well enough alone when you have <i>plenty</i> of alternatives for playing Grand Theft Yeddim already.</div> </div> </div> </div>An argument from authority is not convincing. On top of completely missing my point.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>kindledRadial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/333352-3e-abyssals-exalted-hauntings?p=334866#post334866\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Deathlords in Ex2 were a setting <i>restraint</i> on character concept because they had perfect control over the exaltation process for every abyssal. So White Wolf essentially gave the poorly-written NPC veto power over <i>your</i> character concept. If your storyteller never brought this up with you then either they chose to ignore canon in favor of your character, which was probably wise, or you were playing a loyalist anyway and it never came up. There isn't really a third choice there because if you do obey canon in your game then the Deathlords are impossible to ignore when drafting abyssal characters in Ex2, which again, sucks.</div> </div> </div> </div>The likelihood of this actually being a problem lies totally with the ST. Canon does not mandate a character type like you are saying it does. <br /> <br /> Look, the ST should not be a dick about your concept, unless the ST says &quot;I want to run a game about XYZ&quot; and your character clearly cannot fit into the themes of that game; in that circumstance, it's appropriate for the ST to ask you to build a different character that is more fitting for the game they want to run. But what you're doing here is worrying over a situation that is never going to actually come up IC with an ST who is not a complete asshole, because the ST is also the NPC and the NPC can have reasoning to not just pick another sociopath Killfuck Soulshitter.<br /> <br /> Say you're playing a mortals game where, at some point, all the PCs are supposed to become Abyssals, that this was a long-standing premise of the game and the hook the ST pitched. Say the moment of the mortal's death comes but the NPC skips you over and your character dies. <i>That is a problem with your ST, not the setting</i> (regardless of the poor writing in that part of the setting). No amount of good writing can fix an ST deciding to dick over a player like that; it's a social contract problem, not a bad fluff or bad crunch problem.<br /> <br /> There are a million reasons why Deathlords would Exalt non-stock characters knowing they could get a lot more out of them than a straight-up executed murderer of a Killfuck Soulshitter. Hell, look at some of the canon Abyssals. Melkin Fool in Red comes to mind. <br /> <br /> This is not ignoring canon. Your interpretation of canon is frankly pretty out there in terms of how narrow a range of characters you think the book paints as acceptable and this just is not true. The Deathlords can't see the future. They're not human any more either: they're both more and less than that, they're impossibly old with overinflated egos and that colors their reactions and emotions. They can't foresee that a character who might have accepted the Black Exaltation out of pure fear of death might, within weeks, see what they've signed up for and try to get out.<br /> <br /> The point I agree with you is that getting out is made unreasonably hard with the level of resources each Deathlord controls, but that getting out is probably the impetus to start seeking allies (see: Secret from Keychain of Creation). And I do agree that having the Neverborn exert such control over Deathlords is problematic because individuality doesn't matter when you all have this mandate of KILL CREATION. And it's also boring because practically there's not much difference between &quot;I serve this guy with a massive army who wants to kill the world&quot; with &quot;I serve this really attractive queen who wants to kill the world.&quot;<br /> <br /> I'd like the Neverborn to get shoved into the background like the Yozis are to focus more on the Deathlords as individuals rather than as a template. This of course necessitates lessening the level of control between Neverborn and Deathlord. On that note I am not too worried about the future because if the authors are similarly dissatisfied with how the Neverborn and the Deathlords have been done, how the Abyssal role has been less &quot;apprentice&quot; and more &quot;slave&quot; and there's not a reason to think changes won't be made.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-09T08:36:41-08:00","id":335223,"title":"","content":"I wonder what kindle's thought on the Resonance rule from Shards since I have a feeling that what we got in Ex3 will be closer to that compare to the one in MoEP: Abyssal.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I'd like the Neverborn to get shoved into the background like the Yozis are to focus more on the Deathlords as individuals rather than as a template. This of course necessitates lessening the level of control between Neverborn and Deathlord. On that note I am not too worried about the future because if the authors are similarly dissatisfied with how the Neverborn and the Deathlords have been done, how the Abyssal role has been less &quot;apprentice&quot; and more &quot;slave&quot; and there's not a reason to think changes won't be made. </div> </div> </div>It's always funny how the Neverborn always got described as passive, unable to do anything, except when it involve punishing the PC.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The no.1 fan of Demetheus. I also draw <a href=\"https://probably-unreliable.tumblr.com/tagged/Jenart\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted</a> things and is looking for commission works ~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","name":"Jen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar298_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-09T09:29:36-08:00","id":335244,"title":"","content":"I kind of have a question, outside of whispering terrible, terrible things, dying forever and creating the underworld (by accident) what exactly can the Neverborn do?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I made some Martial Arts for 3e, look at them <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/723442-survival-is-fury-the-monster-reborn-ex3\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> and <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/761356-orgiastic-fugitive-style-3e\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/632-while-my-guitar","name":"While My Guitar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar632_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"606"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-09T09:50:41-08:00","id":335268,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>kindledRadial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/333352-3e-abyssals-exalted-hauntings?p=334911#post334911\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nalak: The Deathlords are varied in many respects but not in this: they would never keep an abyssal they couldn't control. They have no reason to. People die in the millions every day any one of them could make a decent servant. Some of the more experienced deathknights are harder to replace, yes, but that's irrelevant to a starting character. And the Deathlords all have a job to do: end Creation. And <i>they</i> don't have any more choice than <i>you</i> do about that because they are owned part and parcel by the Neverborn. So while one Deathlord might exalt priests and another harlots and another soldiers, when the time comes to get down to business and start razing creation the abyssal that says &quot;no&quot; and stands by it (somehow) is a very very dead Abyssal in canon. It's the same reason people hate the Ex2 Lunar mate dynamics: having an NPC determine your character's actions is awful.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes they probably wouldn't keep someone they didn't think they could control and you know how long a list that is? None. These Deathlords are all egotistical as all heck they are used to being able to make anyone do whatever they want. Hell I had a game once where Mask of Winter actually screwed with one of his abyssals to the point where he went rogue on purpose. He did all of this because the rogue running around gave Winter justification to have his troops go wherever because they're hunting this traitor and Winter is being polite enough to ask for permission for his people to go in and take out this dangerous individual before he starts doing horrible things to their citizens.<br /> <br /> Yes the official order for all the Deathlords is kill reality, but here's what you are getting wrong. The Neverborn just want it done they've never done anything to push the issue on soon. Lion is just amassing an army and trying to build a floating shadowland fortress, Winter is playing politics, The Dowager is just looking into freaking well, and the Bishop has spent god knows how long trying to right a theological argument that will just have people throw themselves into Oblivion. If there is a point where the Deathlords announce &quot;We are going to raze creation go forth or die.&quot; that is literally your ST deciding to do so because canon points out that these guys have been dragging their feet about the big job for millennia. So your argument seems fully based on the premise of &quot;Abyssal exalts should the PCs from Wraith because Wraith was awesome and the Deathlords need to go because my ST won't let us make a character who isn't perfectly inline with themes of a canon one and will instantly execute anyone they even think might go rogue.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-09T10:05:27-08:00","id":335271,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>While My Guitar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/333352-3e-abyssals-exalted-hauntings?p=335244#post335244\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I kind of have a question, outside of whispering terrible, terrible things, dying forever and creating the underworld (by accident) what exactly can the Neverborn do?</div> </div> </div> </div>i think that's kinda the point with them nobody knows how weak or powerful the neverborn really are. we do know that they are as dangerous as chugging yozi venom out of cup made of swinging razor blades that's covered in pyreflame (or whatever that entropy fire that is in the underworld is called), IF you are close to them since First and Forsaken Lions armor didn't merge with him on it's own. but the point is that if your ST decides that the neverborn are capable of demolishing continents using pure force of will then they can do that or alternatively if the ST decides that they can only interact with their servants well then they can't do anything against even a fly as long as it's not a thrall of theirs.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm making the Tales of Exalts webcomic<br /> <a href=\"http://xanroth.deviantart.com/gallery/50854781/tales-of-exalts\" target=\"_blank\">http://xanroth.deviantart.com/galler...ales-of-exalts</a><br /> alchemical report <a href=\"http://xanroth.deviantart.com/gallery/54812164/Alchemical-Report\" target=\"_blank\">http://xanroth.deviantart.com/galler...hemical-Report</a><br /> the fall <a href=\"http://xanroth.deviantart.com/gallery/55265686/the-fall\" target=\"_blank\">http://xanroth.deviantart.com/gallery/55265686/the-fall</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4455-xanroth","name":"Xanroth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4455_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1072"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-09T10:31:49-08:00","id":335316,"title":"","content":"Rater: Okay NOW I think I see the point people are trying to make. Well, I have to concede that I am ramping up the sacrificial factor among Abyssals with this concept. Maybe this could be a flaw at abyssal character creation? So that people could opt in? Or maybe there's a chance of it happening but the roll is similar to when ghosts lose a fetter? Maybe once your work is done the exaltation might move on but leave you alive and resonance free? I would absolutely play an Abyssal with an expiration date but I get that others might not take to it so it shouldn't be the ironclad rule, as was the Deathlord's servitude in Ex2. I think the idea of resonance being a device to keep Abyssals &quot;on task&quot; is a good idea still, though. This would allow abyssal character concepts that aren't &quot;kill everything&quot; that still suffer only minor resonance eruption. It allows you to play what you want and then consider how challenging <i>you</i> want that to be. Thanks for sticking with the thread and putting in your insight.<br /> <br /> Jen: The Shard's version of Resonance rules were a <i>gift</i> and I sincerely hope to see something like them in Ex3 canon. They gave us our first real look at dark abyssal heroes who weren't slaves to the Neverborn and I loved everything I saw there. I use the Shards version of Resonance for all my abyssal renegades.<br /> <br /> Zelbinnean: Well at least we see eye-to-eye on the Neverborn-Deathlord-Abyssal shit-siphon that is Ex2 Underworld canon. And I should clarify that I <i>don't</i> like the level of personal influence the Neverborn have over Resonance and I hope to see that change in Ex3 into something more like it was in Shards. But <i>if you use the shards version</i> then there really is nothing functionally different between the Great Curse and Resonance from an OOC perspective. In fact, I think the Great Curse is much more limiting since it <i>actually</i> mandates your character's actions. Resonance eruptions are always unpleasant but that's <i>it</i> you are tasked as an Abyssal player to overcome unpleasantness. That is the thing which makes them <i>tragic</i> heroes, which is <i>essential</i> to their splat concept and if you think otherwise then I truly think you are missing the point of Abyssals and sincerely hope you play something else in your games. Because without that I personally don't see even one single thing about the Abyssal exaltation worth playing.<br /> <br /> While My Guitar: Not a whole lot. This is one of the problems with them as NPCs: they don't really have anything to do all day <i>except</i> try and end the world. And I just flashed to Neverborn Pinky and Brain there for a moment. Point is: The Neverborn are kinda in need of a rewrite as much as the Deathlords are. As written they may as well still be sleeping, for all the power they unwittingly exert throughout the Underworld and Labyrinth in the death throes of their nightmarish dreams.<br /> <br /> On Ex2 Deathlords: I'm sick and tired of hearing &quot;your storyteller is doing Deathlords wrong&quot; from people, so I'm issuing a challenge: if you think liberating yourself from an E10 Solar-Abyssal hybrid <i>with every charm they qualify for</i> is so fucking easy tell me how <i>you</i> would do this as a starting abyssal and I'll tell you how that doesn't work.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1318-kindledradial","name":"kindledRadial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1318_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-09T11:12:16-08:00","id":335328,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>kindledRadial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/333352-3e-abyssals-exalted-hauntings?p=335316#post335316\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Rater: Okay NOW I think I see the point people are trying to make. Well, I have to concede that I am ramping up the sacrificial factor among Abyssals with this concept. Maybe this could be a flaw at abyssal character creation? So that people could opt in? Or maybe there's a chance of it happening but the roll is similar to when ghosts lose a fetter? Maybe once your work is done the exaltation might move on but leave you alive and resonance free? I would absolutely play an Abyssal with an expiration date but I get that others might not take to it so it shouldn't be the ironclad rule, as was the Deathlord's servitude in Ex2. I think the idea of resonance being a device to keep Abyssals &quot;on task&quot; is a good idea still, though. This would allow abyssal character concepts that aren't &quot;kill everything&quot; that still suffer only minor resonance eruption. It allows you to play what you want and then consider how challenging <i>you</i> want that to be. Thanks for sticking with the thread and putting in your insight.<br /> <br /> Jen: The Shard's version of Resonance rules were a <i>gift</i> and I sincerely hope to see something like them in Ex3 canon. They gave us our first real look at dark abyssal heroes who weren't slaves to the Neverborn and I loved everything I saw there. I use the Shards version of Resonance for all my abyssal renegades.<br /> <br /> Zelbinnean: Well at least we see eye-to-eye on the Neverborn-Deathlord-Abyssal shit-siphon that is Ex2 Underworld canon. And I should clarify that I <i>don't</i> like the level of personal influence the Neverborn have over Resonance and I hope to see that change in Ex3 into something more like it was in Shards. But <i>if you use the shards version</i> then there really is nothing functionally different between the Great Curse and Resonance from an OOC perspective. In fact, I think the Great Curse is much more limiting since it <i>actually</i> mandates your character's actions. Resonance eruptions are always unpleasant but that's <i>it</i> you are tasked as an Abyssal player to overcome unpleasantness. That is the thing which makes them <i>tragic</i> heroes, which is <i>essential</i> to their splat concept and if you think otherwise then I truly think you are missing the point of Abyssals and sincerely hope you play something else in your games. Because without that I personally don't see even one single thing about the Abyssal exaltation worth playing.<br /> <br /> While My Guitar: Not a whole lot. This is one of the problems with them as NPCs: they don't really have anything to do all day <i>except</i> try and end the world. And I just flashed to Neverborn Pinky and Brain there for a moment. Point is: The Neverborn are kinda in need of a rewrite as much as the Deathlords are. As written they may as well still be sleeping, for all the power they unwittingly exert throughout the Underworld and Labyrinth in the death throes of their nightmarish dreams.<br /> <br /> On Ex2 Deathlords: I'm sick and tired of hearing &quot;your storyteller is doing Deathlords wrong&quot; from people, so I'm issuing a challenge: if you think liberating yourself from an E10 Solar-Abyssal hybrid <i>with every charm they qualify for</i> is so fucking easy tell me how <i>you</i> would do this as a starting abyssal and I'll tell you how that doesn't work.</div> </div> </div> </div>It probably depends on the deathlord if you ask me and when the opportunity arrives. example if your deathlord is mask of winter the safest place to hide is amongst his enemies or maybe even just run like hell through shadowlands owned by his rivals because none of the deathlords seems to keen on starting a war with one of the other deathlords and if you are just a new abyssal then it would probably be a waste of resources to hunt you down (this depends on your liege rating i guess) and a foolish thing to go in person since if one of the deathlords started to move about in creation I'm pretty sure a lot of their enemies would take the opportunity to try and strike them down or try and conquer some of their land in the underworld.<br /> <br /> Other than that its just stay far away from their &quot;areas&quot; and you should be fine since the deathlord knows that your exaltion will be back in his/her grasp when you die and with resonance acting like it does and without the protection that a deathlord is capable of providing they will most likely just wait for a wyldhunt to go get you or some other similar thing because the deathlords know that they have all the time in the world to wait.<br /> <br /> sorry about the wall of text","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm making the Tales of Exalts webcomic<br /> <a href=\"http://xanroth.deviantart.com/gallery/50854781/tales-of-exalts\" target=\"_blank\">http://xanroth.deviantart.com/galler...ales-of-exalts</a><br /> alchemical report <a href=\"http://xanroth.deviantart.com/gallery/54812164/Alchemical-Report\" target=\"_blank\">http://xanroth.deviantart.com/galler...hemical-Report</a><br /> the fall <a href=\"http://xanroth.deviantart.com/gallery/55265686/the-fall\" target=\"_blank\">http://xanroth.deviantart.com/gallery/55265686/the-fall</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4455-xanroth","name":"Xanroth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4455_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1072"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-09T11:57:48-08:00","id":335355,"title":"","content":"Xanroth: While you make a good point about hiding in Creation and that the Deathlords can reasonably wait for young deathknights to get themselves killed, I want to point out a couple things.<br /> <br /> 1: Any discussion about free abyssals normally <i>has</i> to begin with destroying your own monstrance, since otherwise our first question becomes &quot;why hasn't your deathlord touched your monstrance and rewritten your personality and/or killed you yet?&quot; because that is what the canon Monstrance allows them to do. So before we even begin to talk about long-term survival remember that just playing this character concept requires that your character destroyed an artifact N/A and then ran off with an irreplaceable abyssal exaltation. That sort of thing does not sit well with the Deathlords. We can assume they will be motivated to get you back.<br /> <br /> 2: Deathlords are <i>NOT</i> shy about starting wars with each other. At all. You would think that the serious implications of a resonance eruption for them would limit this but no, as the Mask and Walker have proven throughout history there is no power that can put a limit on Deathlord pettiness and spite. It would delight <i>any </i> Deathlord to snatch up another's Abyssal exaltation, since this wouldn't count as working against each other (the exaltation was acting disloyally at that point) but an act of reprisal <i>would</i>. So hiding out in another Deathlord's domain is very much out of the soul steel frying pan, into <i>another</i> soulsteel frying pan.<br /> <br /> 3: While Deathlords do have &quot;all the time in the world&quot; they very rarely have the patience to act like it. Case and point, FaFL's invasion of Creation via fairfolk accidentally curing the Great Contagion. They all want the glory. And it is a slap in the face to any of them having a disloyal servant out among their enemies in defiance of their edict. What's more, any patience they <i>might</i> have flies out the window when the Neverborn come calling for results and want a head count on all those abyssal exaltations they were entrusted with. A Deathlord who loses track of an abyssal and has no plan for retrieving them soon is going to be in very serious trouble with their bosses.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1318-kindledradial","name":"kindledRadial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1318_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-09T12:10:27-08:00","id":335365,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>kindledRadial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/333352-3e-abyssals-exalted-hauntings?p=335355#post335355\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Xanroth: While you make a good point about hiding in Creation and that the Deathlords can reasonably wait for young deathknights to get themselves killed, I want to point out a couple things.<br /> <br /> 1: Any discussion about free abyssals normally <i>has</i> to begin with destroying your own monstrance, since otherwise our first question becomes &quot;why hasn't your deathlord touched your monstrance and rewritten your personality and/or killed you yet?&quot; because that is what the canon Monstrance allows them to do. So before we even begin to talk about long-term survival remember that just playing this character concept requires that your character destroyed an artifact N/A and then ran off with an irreplaceable abyssal exaltation. That sort of thing does not sit well with the Deathlords. We can assume they will be motivated to get you back.<br /> <br /> 2: Deathlords are <i>NOT</i> shy about starting wars with each other. At all. You would think that the serious implications of a resonance eruption for them would limit this but no, as the Mask and Walker have proven throughout history there is no power that can put a limit on Deathlord pettiness and spite. It would delight <i>any </i> Deathlord to snatch up another's Abyssal exaltation, since this wouldn't count as working against each other (the exaltation was acting disloyally at that point) but an act of reprisal <i>would</i>. So hiding out in another Deathlord's domain is very much out of the soul steel frying pan, into <i>another</i> soulsteel frying pan.<br /> <br /> 3: While Deathlords do have &quot;all the time in the world&quot; they very rarely have the patience to act like it. Case and point, FaFL's invasion of Creation via fairfolk accidentally curing the Great Contagion. They all want the glory. And it is a slap in the face to any of them having a disloyal servant out among their enemies in defiance of their edict. What's more, any patience they <i>might</i> have flies out the window when the Neverborn come calling for results and want a head count on all those abyssal exaltations they were entrusted with. A Deathlord who loses track of an abyssal and has no plan for retrieving them soon is going to be in very serious trouble with their bosses.</div> </div> </div> </div>1: hmm i did not know that they could kill you through the monstrance far as i know all they could do is use the scream in silence charm on it and yell at you or dunk it in the void which would only restore your willpower if you follow the errata, haven't seen anything about them being able to rewrite people because if they could then i would have thought the bohdisatva would have done that to that wolf guy whatever his name is.<br /> <br /> 2: didn't the last war between deathlords end up with fafl getting permanently locked in his armor and pretty much sent of to the time out corner of creation? haven't really looked all that much into what wars Mr mask have been up too but far as i know he just have a few skirmishes with the walker after he went and threw subterfuge out the window into the void and captured Thornes.<br /> <br /> 3: didn't the lion and eye do that to prevent the end of the world since so far it seems like only the dowager actually tries to do what the neverborn wants them to do the others does the same thing the other ghosts does aka repeat the things they did in life.<br /> also I'm pretty sure the neverborn doesn't give a damn about if an abyssal is under deathlord control or just running around in creation because no matter if its a psycho that ran cause his lord told him to stop stabbing children or a saint who ran cause his lord said start stabbing children thanks to resonance both will make life suck for everyone around them","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm making the Tales of Exalts webcomic<br /> <a href=\"http://xanroth.deviantart.com/gallery/50854781/tales-of-exalts\" target=\"_blank\">http://xanroth.deviantart.com/galler...ales-of-exalts</a><br /> alchemical report <a href=\"http://xanroth.deviantart.com/gallery/54812164/Alchemical-Report\" target=\"_blank\">http://xanroth.deviantart.com/galler...hemical-Report</a><br /> the fall <a href=\"http://xanroth.deviantart.com/gallery/55265686/the-fall\" target=\"_blank\">http://xanroth.deviantart.com/gallery/55265686/the-fall</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4455-xanroth","name":"Xanroth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4455_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1072"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-09T12:24:35-08:00","id":335376,"title":"","content":"As a point of clarification, the Deathlord doesn't have any explicit power to kill the Abyssal via touching the monstrance, but any Abyssal who still has a Monstrance of Celestial Portion can be affected by sorcery/necromancy spells via the Monstrance as an arcane link.<br /> <br /> Keeping in mind of course that for more than a few spells, merely possessing an arcane link to the target does neither jack nor shit; Flying Guillotine doesn't care if you have a lock of the target's hair.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-09T12:26:19-08:00","id":335378,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/333352-3e-abyssals-exalted-hauntings?p=335376#post335376\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As a point of clarification, the Deathlord doesn't have any explicit power to kill the Abyssal via touching the monstrance, but any Abyssal who still has a Monstrance of Celestial Portion can be affected by sorcery/necromancy spells via the Monstrance as an arcane link.<br /> <br /> Keeping in mind of course that for more than a few spells, merely possessing an arcane link to the target does neither jack nor shit; Flying Guillotine doesn't care if you have a lock of the target's hair.</div> </div> </div> </div>thank you kindly for the clarification good sir much appreciated","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm making the Tales of Exalts webcomic<br /> <a href=\"http://xanroth.deviantart.com/gallery/50854781/tales-of-exalts\" target=\"_blank\">http://xanroth.deviantart.com/galler...ales-of-exalts</a><br /> alchemical report <a href=\"http://xanroth.deviantart.com/gallery/54812164/Alchemical-Report\" target=\"_blank\">http://xanroth.deviantart.com/galler...hemical-Report</a><br /> the fall <a href=\"http://xanroth.deviantart.com/gallery/55265686/the-fall\" target=\"_blank\">http://xanroth.deviantart.com/gallery/55265686/the-fall</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4455-xanroth","name":"Xanroth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4455_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1072"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-09T12:42:21-08:00","id":335386,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/333352-3e-abyssals-exalted-hauntings?p=335376#post335376\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As a point of clarification, the Deathlord doesn't have any explicit power to kill the Abyssal via touching the monstrance, but any Abyssal who still has a Monstrance of Celestial Portion can be affected by sorcery/necromancy spells via the Monstrance as an arcane link.</div> </div> </div> </div>It also counts as touching the Abyssal for purposes of charm use. So any charm with the touch keyword can be used on them remotely.<br /> <br /> Even without that though an Abyssal without a perfect shaping defense can still be spammed with Void-tier necromancy that separates flesh from bone, and everyone else can be perfectly tracked at any time for a timely hecatonkhire or Abyssal death squad assault, which is assuming that your Deathlord stays too busy to visit you themselves.<br /> <br /> Basically, imagine if the Wyld Hunt always knew exactly where you were, knew everything about you and your exaltation, had nearly infinite resources and nothing else better to do than hunt you down. That's about the level of resources a monstrance gives a Deathlord.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1318-kindledradial","name":"kindledRadial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1318_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-09T12:48:49-08:00","id":335392,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>kindledRadial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/333352-3e-abyssals-exalted-hauntings?p=335386#post335386\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It also counts as touching the Abyssal for purposes of charm use. So any charm with the touch keyword can be used on them remotely.<br /> <br /> Even without that though an Abyssal without a perfect shaping defense can still be spammed with Void-tier necromancy that separates flesh from bone, and everyone else can be perfectly tracked at any time for a timely hecatonkhire or Abyssal death squad assault, which is assuming that your Deathlord stays too busy to visit you themselves.<br /> <br /> Basically, imagine if the Wyld Hunt always knew exactly where you were, knew everything about you and your exaltation, had nearly infinite resources and nothing else better to do than hunt you down. That's about the level of resources a monstrance gives a Deathlord.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> hmm sounds a bit like a waste of resources to do that to a low level abyssal and probably not enough against a high level one.<br /> also a deathlord could most likely just let a death knight go if it fits his scheme example fafle might let a powerful dusk warlord amass an army and try and take him down just so he can have a proper enemy to test his army against... or just for shits and giggles in the case of some deathlords cause remember they all have their own agenda","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm making the Tales of Exalts webcomic<br /> <a href=\"http://xanroth.deviantart.com/gallery/50854781/tales-of-exalts\" target=\"_blank\">http://xanroth.deviantart.com/galler...ales-of-exalts</a><br /> alchemical report <a href=\"http://xanroth.deviantart.com/gallery/54812164/Alchemical-Report\" target=\"_blank\">http://xanroth.deviantart.com/galler...hemical-Report</a><br /> the fall <a href=\"http://xanroth.deviantart.com/gallery/55265686/the-fall\" target=\"_blank\">http://xanroth.deviantart.com/gallery/55265686/the-fall</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4455-xanroth","name":"Xanroth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4455_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1072"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-09T12:58:32-08:00","id":335397,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>kindledRadial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/333352-3e-abyssals-exalted-hauntings?p=335386#post335386\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Even without that though an Abyssal without a perfect shaping defense can still be spammed with Void-tier necromancy that separates flesh from bone, and everyone else can be perfectly tracked at any time for a timely hecatonkhire or Abyssal death squad assault, which is assuming that your Deathlord stays too busy to visit you themselves.</div> </div> </div> </div>The list of Void Circle spells doesn't have any that can be delivered via arcane link, so if this happens, it wouldn't be figurative language to say that the ST is inventing a spell for the purpose of punishing you. In fact, the only offensive spells that require an arcane link to target are Dead Man's Voice, Shadow Summons, Silent Words of Dreams and Nightmares, Bone Lion, Insidious Tendrils of Hate, and Wrath of the Five Elements (which needs two more, one of which must explicitly come from the target's body, and is also Solar Circle so not something a Deathlord can deploy). Not a one of these is insurmountable.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>kindledRadial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/333352-3e-abyssals-exalted-hauntings?p=335386#post335386\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Basically, imagine if the Wyld Hunt always knew exactly where you were, knew everything about you and your exaltation, had nearly infinite resources and nothing else better to do than hunt you down. That's about the level of resources a monstrance gives a Deathlord.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Nothing else better to do?&quot; Obviously we've got a problem, considering your previous paragraph &quot;assum[ed] that your Deathlord stays too busy to visit you themselves.&quot; Either he's busy or he's not busy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 12-09-2014, 04:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-09T13:03:24-08:00","id":335400,"title":"","content":"It's true that the easiest way to play a free abyssal in Ex2 is to be free &quot;as the Deathlord intended&quot; but I personally don't find that very fun from a player perspective. Either you enter into it with the foreknowledge that this was planned which feels kinda weak or you don't know and then your ST springs this on you later which is very disempowering. Although do like the idea of a Moonshadow locked in a game of wits with their Deathlord as they via to establish control over each other in a series of convoluted schemes ala &quot;you thought that was your <i>real</i> monstrance??&quot;<br /> <br /> As for resources, again, this is an Abyssal exaltation we're talking about. It's an Artifact N/A that can never be replaced, is highly desired by their enemies and could eventually turn on them to wreck meaningful harm on their plans. Some Deathlords are egomaniacal enough to play god with them anyway, yes, but none of them are stupid. If part of your character's motivation puts them at meaningful odds with their Deathlord's plans their response should be swift and effective because they have the means to make it so and no real cause to play nice.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1318-kindledradial","name":"kindledRadial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1318_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-09T13:32:28-08:00","id":335438,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>kindledRadial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/333352-3e-abyssals-exalted-hauntings?p=335400#post335400\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's true that the easiest way to play a free abyssal in Ex2 is to be free &quot;as the Deathlord intended&quot; but I personally don't find that very fun from a player perspective. Either you enter into it with the foreknowledge that this was planned which feels kinda weak or you don't know and then your ST springs this on you later which is very disempowering. Although do like the idea of a Moonshadow locked in a game of wits with their Deathlord as they via to establish control over each other in a series of convoluted schemes ala &quot;you thought that was your <i>real</i> monstrance??&quot;<br /> <br /> As for resources, again, this is an Abyssal exaltation we're talking about. It's an Artifact N/A that can never be replaced, is highly desired by their enemies and could eventually turn on them to wreck meaningful harm on their plans. Some Deathlords are egomaniacal enough to play god with them anyway, yes, but none of them are stupid. If part of your character's motivation puts them at meaningful odds with their Deathlord's plans their response should be swift and effective because they have the means to make it so and no real cause to play nice.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> sounds like you may have had a bad experience with being free as the deathlord intended scenario because if its pulled of right i can lead to some pretty cool stuff example cross campaign things like maybe you stopped another abyssal from getting an artifact that would have opened up a shadowland at this or that place and this might have happened when your character was brand new but now you are like essence 6 or something and confronting your deathlord suddenly he thanks you for stopping his rivals plan to use that artifact to open a shadowland and now you will suddenly think &quot;have everything I've done been his plan all along?&quot; it might feel disempowering it might feel cool as a player BUT now its up to you to use this, use it and react the way your character would react. would he be angry and rage? would he break down at this sudden reveal? that is the power that such events can lead to. who cares if you can throw mountains or swim in lava if you don't get in character its just like any video game. i mean no offence or anything like that i have a few syndromes that sometimes makes me a bit well untactful about things so i apologize if i have offended in any way.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm making the Tales of Exalts webcomic<br /> <a href=\"http://xanroth.deviantart.com/gallery/50854781/tales-of-exalts\" target=\"_blank\">http://xanroth.deviantart.com/galler...ales-of-exalts</a><br /> alchemical report <a href=\"http://xanroth.deviantart.com/gallery/54812164/Alchemical-Report\" target=\"_blank\">http://xanroth.deviantart.com/galler...hemical-Report</a><br /> the fall <a href=\"http://xanroth.deviantart.com/gallery/55265686/the-fall\" target=\"_blank\">http://xanroth.deviantart.com/gallery/55265686/the-fall</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4455-xanroth","name":"Xanroth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4455_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1072"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-09T13:43:55-08:00","id":335447,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>kindledRadial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/333352-3e-abyssals-exalted-hauntings?p=335316#post335316\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But <i>if you use the shards version</i> then there really is nothing functionally different between the Great Curse and Resonance from an OOC perspective.</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe, but I'll wager many fewer people are actually familiar with the Shards version vs the MOEP version, and certainly the MOEP version was the only option for most of the life of the line and is the default in normal Creation stories, so most people will think of it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>kindledRadial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/333352-3e-abyssals-exalted-hauntings?p=335316#post335316\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In fact, I think the Great Curse is much more limiting since it <i>actually</i> mandates your character's actions.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah this is just as problematic. It doesn't inspire the ability to tell a player &quot;okay here is your scene having a mythic psychotic break&quot; when it actually tells you how you act, with the intent being &quot;you shave your head and run off to meditate on a mountain, but only for a weekend because to do otherwise would fuck up the story too much.&quot; That itself is an insane justification versus, I dunno, removing moral limits or setting a new defining character facet or something else. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>kindledRadial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/333352-3e-abyssals-exalted-hauntings?p=335316#post335316\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That is the thing which makes them <i>tragic</i> heroes, which is <i>essential</i> to their splat concept and if you think otherwise then I truly think you are missing the point of Abyssals and sincerely hope you play something else in your games. Because without that I personally don't see even one single thing about the Abyssal exaltation worth playing.</div> </div> </div> </div>The intent of Resonance may be to help you play a tragic hero. The actual reality of Resonance does not really support that kind of game because of how players respond to what comes across as arbitrarily being beaten about the head and shoulders (which is how Resonance comes across). If anything Resonance encourages you to be a psycho loner to game how much spiritual injury you're actually going to face (much like how Virtues themselves basically let you game your personality and leverage mechanical benefit from it, which was a totally shitty idea: personality should not be mechanically optimizable, ffs).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>kindledRadial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/333352-3e-abyssals-exalted-hauntings?p=335316#post335316\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On Ex2 Deathlords: I'm sick and tired of hearing &quot;your storyteller is doing Deathlords wrong&quot; from people, so I'm issuing a challenge: if you think liberating yourself from an E10 Solar-Abyssal hybrid <i>with every charm they qualify for</i> is so fucking easy tell me how <i>you</i> would do this as a starting abyssal and I'll tell you how that doesn't work.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well yeah man. Deathlord crunch is lazy and awful, especially post-Dreams where high-Essence Charms are more than just theory craft. I don't think people were really saying that. The most logical explanation is for a Deathlord to allow it out of a Just As Planned style Xanatos Gambit, which in itself is pretty crappy because it actually removes the PC's own agency and decision making; it was all part of a chess move by a King of Games and thus is completely planned. Which can be cool one time, but as a default it totally sucks.<br /> <br /> My point was that there's not a reason to believe that having a Deathward functionally limits your character personality options at chargen, unless you ST is being a dick about it. Because Deathlords are still quirky individuals who might see value in Exalting a stabbed cheating gambler over yet another psychotic child-murderer. In this scenario yes it's best to ignore all high-Essence Charms because they actively did a fuckton more harm than good to the setting and to fundamental setting assumptions.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>kindledRadial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/333352-3e-abyssals-exalted-hauntings?p=335386#post335386\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It also counts as touching the Abyssal for purposes of charm use. So any charm with the touch keyword can be used on them remotely.<br /> <br /> Even without that though an Abyssal without a perfect shaping defense can still be spammed with Void-tier necromancy that separates flesh from bone, and everyone else can be perfectly tracked at any time for a timely hecatonkhire or Abyssal death squad assault, which is assuming that your Deathlord stays too busy to visit you themselves.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay we all know 2e heavy-Keyword crunch is total shit and not fun to play. Actually discussing 2e crunch is really not productive versus discussing the kinds of themes and hypothetical controls a Monstrance might provide. Like, I'm fine with an arcane link but anything beyond that is clearly just a shit sandwich and deprotagonizing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-09T13:52:31-08:00","id":335450,"title":"","content":"I feel I should weigh in a bit as I am kindle's storyteller. There have been 2 major representations of the struggle of independence one was under the service to a non canon deathlord who his service eventually cost him much of what he cared for in mass destruction of innocents and the other who went renegade by committing mass sabotage on his lords geomancy construction system beginning a manhunt and destruction of much of the underworld under various power struggles","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1166-korekore","name":"korekore","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1166_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"141"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-09T13:54:37-08:00","id":335452,"title":"","content":"I have portrayed them as being very well informed, genius intellects, and obscenely proud and unable to consider certain roads of action allowing abyssals to get the drop on them or surprise them. I did play with the ability to affect with the touch keyword through a monstrous which prompted a lot of questions due to some of the charms that have that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1166-korekore","name":"korekore","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1166_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"141"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-09T13:58:17-08:00","id":335457,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>korekore</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/333352-3e-abyssals-exalted-hauntings?p=335452#post335452\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have portrayed them as being very well informed, genius intellects, and obscenely proud and unable to consider certain roads of action allowing abyssals to get the drop on them or surprise them. I did play with the ability to affect with the touch keyword through a monstrous which prompted a lot of questions due to some of the charms that have that.</div> </div> </div> </div>ok that explains a lot actually i personally think its cool that you used one of the unnamed deathlords and it sounds like you did a good job portraying how evil deathlords can be and i mean its not bloody likely that fafle will be handing out cookies","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm making the Tales of Exalts webcomic<br /> <a href=\"http://xanroth.deviantart.com/gallery/50854781/tales-of-exalts\" target=\"_blank\">http://xanroth.deviantart.com/galler...ales-of-exalts</a><br /> alchemical report <a href=\"http://xanroth.deviantart.com/gallery/54812164/Alchemical-Report\" target=\"_blank\">http://xanroth.deviantart.com/galler...hemical-Report</a><br /> the fall <a href=\"http://xanroth.deviantart.com/gallery/55265686/the-fall\" target=\"_blank\">http://xanroth.deviantart.com/gallery/55265686/the-fall</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4455-xanroth","name":"Xanroth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4455_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1072"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-09T15:53:15-08:00","id":335546,"title":"","content":"Honestly even when he pissed one off they didn't just off him, they just ruined his life, he played someone very pro ghosts and ghost rights, his friends ended up as soulsteel cutlery that would be left under his daughters pillow, his name was bismurched by a crafted look alike using his name who assaulted and razed one of the independent ghost nations subjecting a ghost blood friend of his's mother to vile toture so when she next saw him she tried to kill him. Things like that. Killing him would have been a mercy","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1166-korekore","name":"korekore","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1166_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"141"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-09T16:59:39-08:00","id":335584,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>kindledRadial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/333352-3e-abyssals-exalted-hauntings?p=335386#post335386\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It also counts as touching the Abyssal for purposes of charm use. So any charm with the touch keyword can be used on them remotely.</div> </div> </div> </div>The second part is actually untrue. It works like that only for <i>some</i> charms, all of which must have it specified in their description. Offhand i can remember only one, which is used for communication.<br /> Also, remember that if the Abyssal were to die as a result of a charm or necromancy spell used through Monstrance, it would shatter and the Exaltation would go free. Recovering it would be a problem, with a serious possibility that some other Deathlord might grab it first.<br /> (And pre 2.5 errata, mind influence would be a problem, seeing as Abyssals had perfect mental defence effect that caused resonance back on attacker. And it was mentioned that Resonance eruptions for deathlords were way more nasty than for abyssals. Though that effect was almost certainly not intended)<br /> Yes, Monstrance was a big problem (especially since the arcane link could possibly be used to <i>track</i> the renegade), but let's not try to add to it by inventing new non-canon rules. Unless of course it's GM's intention to really screw players over - and players are perfectly okay with it.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><i>The difference between fiction and reality? Fiction has to make sense.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/434-astralporing","name":"Astralporing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar434_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"296"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-09T19:23:17-08:00","id":335676,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/333352-3e-abyssals-exalted-hauntings?p=335447#post335447\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well yeah man. Deathlord crunch is lazy and awful, especially post-Dreams where high-Essence Charms are more than just theory craft. I don't think people were really saying that. The most logical explanation is for a Deathlord to allow it out of a Just As Planned style Xanatos Gambit, which in itself is pretty crappy because it actually removes the PC's own agency and decision making; it was all part of a chess move by a King of Games and thus is completely planned. Which can be cool one time, but as a default it totally sucks.<br /> <br /> My point was that there's not a reason to believe that having a Deathward functionally limits your character personality options at chargen, unless you ST is being a dick about it. Because Deathlords are still quirky individuals who might see value in Exalting a stabbed cheating gambler over yet another psychotic child-murderer. In this scenario yes it's best to ignore all high-Essence Charms because they actively did a fuckton more harm than good to the setting and to fundamental setting assumptions.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's also that if you're really going with 2e's mechanics and Deathlords who are just that powerful as justification, and you are just as confident the Deathlords are truly, sincerely trying to end the world,* you kinda have to sweep most of this discussion aside entirely. This is because you have a much bigger question to answer of how the world existed long enough for the question of Deathlords with Abyssals to even come up. If the Deathlords were as motivated, determined, and powerful as posited, one of them would have Creation-Slaying Oblivion Kick'd everything into the Void a very long time ago. One or all of those factors can't fit.<br /> <br /> * For the record, with exceptions, this is a questionable assumption.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-09T19:39:43-08:00","id":335703,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gaius</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/333352-3e-abyssals-exalted-hauntings?p=335676#post335676\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's also that if you're really going with 2e's mechanics and Deathlords who are just that powerful as justification, and you are just as confident the Deathlords are truly, sincerely trying to end the world,* you kinda have to sweep most of this discussion aside entirely. This is because you have a much bigger question to answer of how the world existed long enough for the question of Deathlords with Abyssals to even come up. If the Deathlords were as motivated, determined, and powerful as posited, one of them would have Creation-Slaying Oblivion Kick'd everything into the Void a very long time ago. One or all of those factors can't fit.<br /> <br /> * For the record, with exceptions, this is a questionable assumption.</div> </div> </div> </div>Exactly. And the notion of Creation-Slaying Oblivion Kick predated the first release of Dreams, IIRC, because all it requires is a particular SMA (not unreasonable for a Deathlord to know in their life) and a Solar Charm that lets you see to the horizon. Dreams (and its errata, which was good and needed, but still a whole different game than what was envisioned in the Core) just made other RAW assumptions about the Deathlords, among them the possibility of CSOK (which they certainly would have access to, and with easier ways than SMA), worse and more implausible.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":3420,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","user":"Zelbinnean","date":". 12-09-2014, 10:55 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-09T23:31:35-08:00","id":335846,"title":"","content":"In kortekore's defense, I am <i>infamous</i> in every game I play for racking up unintentional collateral damage. The whole &quot;nuking an entire metropolis&quot; thing was very much avoidable, I just made one or two fatal tactical mistakes...<br /> <br /> Zelbinnean: It sounds like we both agree that serious mistakes were made in binding and gagging abyssal character themes to the notion of &quot;Deathlord's whipping boy.&quot; I still want Abyssal characters to face sacrifices in game, but I want those sacrifices to be varied and not always rooted in &quot;evil king NPC is feeling spiteful today.&quot; If you took away the Deathlords entirely (or just wrote them better) then most of what you're saying bothers you with regards to Resonance goes away, I think. I see a lot of problems with MoEP:A in that regard as well. So maybe we are actually on a similar page there. Unfortunately, fixing the Deathlords is a massive undertaking such that I don't think we can really address it in this thread. My fingers are crossed Onyx Path will pull it off in Ex3 though.<br /> <br /> Xanroth: I'm coming around to the idea of a game where you are part of your Deathlord's running joke, but I still don't like how few alternatives to that remain in Ex2 for playing renegades. As written any time you and a Deathlord square off and they feel like being even a little bit serious you should die by rights, and the abyssal exaltation is just too valuable a thing to ignore forever. At that point your character's survival hinges on seeming &quot;cute&quot; to your Deathlord which is kind of not that satisfying when you know that if you ever <i>do</i> manage to severely hurt your nemesis the immediate result is probably certain death. This actually comes back to the earlier criticism of my own idea: it's not a very fun game when &quot;winning&quot; equates to &quot;can't play that character anymore.&quot;<br /> <br /> Astralporing: Can you post page numbers referencing these rules on &quot;some touch effects&quot; and especially about the monstrance shattering if the exalt dies? That <i>really</i> does not sound right to me, to be honest. I was under the firm impression that the monstrance was where the abyssal exaltation auto-parked when it wasn't in use.<br /> <br /> General: As much as the Deathlords are imbalanced v Abyssals they are somewhat balanced on the &quot;us versus Creation&quot; front by the <i>everything else</i> that would resist them. Like I'm willing to believe that the collected might of Creation could perma-kill these guys as written in Ex2, if motivated to do so. The thing is that they are <i>smart</i> so they haven't made any half-hearted attempts to follow through on that plan which would bump them up to the top of several Incarna's &quot;kill now&quot; list. Like the last time they gave it a serious go was the Great Contagion which damn near <i>worked</i> and only didn't because they got in <i>each other's </i>way. Since then they've gone back to the proverbial drawing board so we probably won't see another attempt for a couple centuries or so in canon.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1318-kindledradial","name":"kindledRadial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1318_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-10T00:12:56-08:00","id":335876,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>korekore</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/333352-3e-abyssals-exalted-hauntings?p=335546#post335546\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Honestly even when he pissed one off they didn't just off him, they just ruined his life, he played someone very pro ghosts and ghost rights, his friends ended up as soulsteel cutlery that would be left under his daughters pillow, his name was bismurched by a crafted look alike using his name who assaulted and razed one of the independent ghost nations subjecting a ghost blood friend of his's mother to vile toture so when she next saw him she tried to kill him. Things like that. Killing him would have been a mercy</div> </div> </div> </div>bravo, that is EXACTLY how the deathlords should act they don't just kill you of because that's not a punishment when you are a deathlord already dead and more powerful than ever pretty much.<br /> i mean one example of how a deathlord punishes abyssals is one that will appear in the comic I'm making so i wont spoil anything here but lets just say he was happy then he got a pair of swords now he's empty.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm making the Tales of Exalts webcomic<br /> <a href=\"http://xanroth.deviantart.com/gallery/50854781/tales-of-exalts\" target=\"_blank\">http://xanroth.deviantart.com/galler...ales-of-exalts</a><br /> alchemical report <a href=\"http://xanroth.deviantart.com/gallery/54812164/Alchemical-Report\" target=\"_blank\">http://xanroth.deviantart.com/galler...hemical-Report</a><br /> the fall <a href=\"http://xanroth.deviantart.com/gallery/55265686/the-fall\" target=\"_blank\">http://xanroth.deviantart.com/gallery/55265686/the-fall</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4455-xanroth","name":"Xanroth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4455_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1072"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-10T05:39:05-08:00","id":336006,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>kindledRadial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/333352-3e-abyssals-exalted-hauntings?p=335846#post335846\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Astralporing: Can you post page numbers referencing these rules on &quot;some touch effects&quot; and especially about the monstrance shattering if the exalt dies? That <i>really</i> does not sound right to me, to be honest. I was under the firm impression that the monstrance was where the abyssal exaltation auto-parked when it wasn't in use.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's not &quot;some touch effects&quot;. It's &quot;some charms&quot; with no further explanation, and the only charm i know having it flat out specified in the charm description. And it's right in the Monstrance's writeup (page 117 of MoEP: Abyssals).<br /> <br /> &quot;Arcane Link: Certain Abyssal Charms (and all necromancy spells) treat a deathknight\u2019s Monstrance as if it were a physical extension of her body, transmitting the effects of the magic directly to her. Deathlords use this dread mystical correspondence to communicate with and punish their deathknights, and to appear in visions to candidates who have not yet chosen whether to die or accept Exaltation. If such effects kill an Abyssal, the cage shatters and the freed Exaltation must be summoned to a new Monstrance. The possibility that another Deathlord might poach the Exaltation, however, usually deters such extreme solutions to treachery.&quot;<br /> <br /> See as it does not specify any <i>class</i> of charms - only say that <i>some</i> of them have that ability. And it uses a known term (&quot;arcane link&quot;) that has a specific meaning when socery and necromancy are concerned (and that meaning is not &quot;you can cast <b>any</b> spell through it as if the target was there&quot;).<br /> <br /> Also, to &quot;summon an exaltation to a new Monstrance&quot; you need to capture that exaltation first. This generally means capturing (alive) its current bearer and placing physically within the Monstrance.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><i>The difference between fiction and reality? Fiction has to make sense.</i>","edited":{"userid":434,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/434-astralporing","user":"Astralporing","date":". 12-10-2014, 08:42 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/434-astralporing","name":"Astralporing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar434_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"296"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-10T06:42:31-08:00","id":336020,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Astralporing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/333352-3e-abyssals-exalted-hauntings?p=336006#post336006\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's not &quot;some touch effects&quot;. It's &quot;some charms&quot; with no further explanation, and the only charm i know having it flat out specified in the charm description. And it's right in the Monstrance's writeup (page 117 of MoEP: Abyssals).<br /> <br /> &quot;Arcane Link: Certain Abyssal Charms (and all necromancy spells) treat a deathknight\u2019s Monstrance as if it were a physical extension of her body, transmitting the effects of the magic directly to her. Deathlords use this dread mystical correspondence to communicate with and punish their deathknights, and to appear in visions to candidates who have not yet chosen whether to die or accept Exaltation. If such effects kill an Abyssal, the cage shatters and the freed Exaltation must be summoned to a new Monstrance. The possibility that another Deathlord might poach the Exaltation, however, usually deters such extreme solutions to treachery.&quot;<br /> <br /> See as it does not specify any <i>class</i> of charms - only say that <i>some</i> of them have that ability. And it uses a known term (&quot;arcane link&quot;) that has a specific meaning when socery and necromancy are concerned (and that meaning is not &quot;you can cast <b>any</b> spell through it as if the target was there&quot;).<br /> <br /> Also, to &quot;summon an exaltation to a new Monstrance&quot; you need to capture that exaltation first. This generally means capturing (alive) its current bearer and placing physically within the Monstrance.</div> </div> </div> </div>i think that might have been erratad","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm making the Tales of Exalts webcomic<br /> <a href=\"http://xanroth.deviantart.com/gallery/50854781/tales-of-exalts\" target=\"_blank\">http://xanroth.deviantart.com/galler...ales-of-exalts</a><br /> alchemical report <a href=\"http://xanroth.deviantart.com/gallery/54812164/Alchemical-Report\" target=\"_blank\">http://xanroth.deviantart.com/galler...hemical-Report</a><br /> the fall <a href=\"http://xanroth.deviantart.com/gallery/55265686/the-fall\" target=\"_blank\">http://xanroth.deviantart.com/gallery/55265686/the-fall</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4455-xanroth","name":"Xanroth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4455_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1072"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-10T09:33:20-08:00","id":336095,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Xanroth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/333352-3e-abyssals-exalted-hauntings?p=336020#post336020\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">i think that might have been erratad</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't see any relevant changes in the scroll of errata i have (the 2.5E version). Unless you mean the last part (summon exaltation to the monstrance) Where Summon the Black Sun is specifically mentioned as non-canon.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><i>The difference between fiction and reality? Fiction has to make sense.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/434-astralporing","name":"Astralporing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar434_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"296"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-10T10:01:10-08:00","id":336127,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Astralporing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/333352-3e-abyssals-exalted-hauntings?p=336095#post336095\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't see any relevant changes in the scroll of errata i have (the 2.5E version). Unless you mean the last part (summon exaltation to the monstrance) Where Summon the Black Sun is specifically mentioned as non-canon.</div> </div> </div> </div>that's probably it, but I'm sure i read somewhere that deathlords killing abyssals through the monstrance was just a lie made bye the deathlords to control the deathknights but it might just be my brain mixing things together","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm making the Tales of Exalts webcomic<br /> <a href=\"http://xanroth.deviantart.com/gallery/50854781/tales-of-exalts\" target=\"_blank\">http://xanroth.deviantart.com/galler...ales-of-exalts</a><br /> alchemical report <a href=\"http://xanroth.deviantart.com/gallery/54812164/Alchemical-Report\" target=\"_blank\">http://xanroth.deviantart.com/galler...hemical-Report</a><br /> the fall <a href=\"http://xanroth.deviantart.com/gallery/55265686/the-fall\" target=\"_blank\">http://xanroth.deviantart.com/gallery/55265686/the-fall</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4455-xanroth","name":"Xanroth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4455_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1072"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-10T11:15:54-08:00","id":336170,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Xanroth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/333352-3e-abyssals-exalted-hauntings?p=336127#post336127\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">that's probably it, but I'm sure i read somewhere that deathlords killing abyssals through the monstrance was just a lie made bye the deathlords to control the deathknights but it might just be my brain mixing things together</div> </div> </div> </div>You might be thinking about the one where Deathlords could supposedly kill an abyssal by throwing the monstance into oblivion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-10T11:28:08-08:00","id":336177,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nalak42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/333352-3e-abyssals-exalted-hauntings?p=336170#post336170\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You might be thinking about the one where Deathlords could supposedly kill an abyssal by throwing the monstance into oblivion.</div> </div> </div> </div>ah that's the one","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm making the Tales of Exalts webcomic<br /> <a href=\"http://xanroth.deviantart.com/gallery/50854781/tales-of-exalts\" target=\"_blank\">http://xanroth.deviantart.com/galler...ales-of-exalts</a><br /> alchemical report <a href=\"http://xanroth.deviantart.com/gallery/54812164/Alchemical-Report\" target=\"_blank\">http://xanroth.deviantart.com/galler...hemical-Report</a><br /> the fall <a href=\"http://xanroth.deviantart.com/gallery/55265686/the-fall\" target=\"_blank\">http://xanroth.deviantart.com/gallery/55265686/the-fall</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4455-xanroth","name":"Xanroth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4455_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1072"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-10T17:40:59-08:00","id":336513,"title":"","content":"Astralporing: Thanks for the reference I looked it up myself and you're right, using a monstrance to kill an exalt <i>directly</i> does ruin the monstrance. I would say though that this is very little deterrent for a Deathlord committed to the task, since they can still use an active monstrance to track an abyssal and kill them through any <i>indirect</i> means (summoned horrors, social attacks lined with suicidal orders, even disease effects, arguably) and the exaltation will zip right back to the coffin. So it adds a step, basically, but again if you ever <i>really</i> offend your specter patron you are looking at a pretty immediate death sentence. You might have a few days to gather your allies and plan a raid to destroy your monstrance but it's still a necessary step.<br /> <br /> General: The actual wording is that such charms and all necromancy spells treat the monstrance &quot;as if it were a physical extension of her body, transmitting the effects of the magic directly to her.&quot; So Pestilence-Bearing Touch still works, since if you affect one part of an exalt's body with the great contagion it <i>will</i> spread to the rest of her, for example. By that same token I would say things that hurt the monstrance still probably hurt you, at the very least insofar as carrying over wound penalties form being <i>on fire</i> on one part of your body. Honestly thereis <i>some </i>room for interpretation here but not much and it doesn't in any way stop them from crippling you creatively and indefinitely.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1318-kindledradial","name":"kindledRadial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1318_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-10T17:49:46-08:00","id":336518,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>kindledRadial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/333352-3e-abyssals-exalted-hauntings?p=336513#post336513\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Astralporing: Thanks for the reference I looked it up myself and you're right, using a monstrance to kill an exalt <i>directly</i> does ruin the monstrance. I would say though that this is very little deterrent for a Deathlord committed to the task, since they can still use an active monstrance to track an abyssal and kill them through any <i>indirect</i> means (summoned horrors, social attacks lined with suicidal orders, even disease effects, arguably) and the exaltation will zip right back to the coffin. So it adds a step, basically, but again if you ever <i>really</i> offend your specter patron you are looking at a pretty immediate death sentence. You might have a few days to gather your allies and plan a raid to destroy your monstrance but it's still a necessary step.<br /> <br /> General: The actual wording is that such charms and all necromancy spells treat the monstrance &quot;as if it were a physical extension of her body, transmitting the effects of the magic directly to her.&quot; So Pestilence-Bearing Touch still works, since if you affect one part of an exalt's body with the great contagion it <i>will</i> spread to the rest of her, for example. By that same token I would say things that hurt the monstrance still probably hurt you, at the very least insofar as carrying over wound penalties form being <i>on fire</i> on one part of your body. Honestly thereis <i>some </i>room for interpretation here but not much and it doesn't in any way stop them from crippling you creatively and indefinitely.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Just a note. Errata made it that destroying the monstrance does nothing to the Abyssal except maybe let them feel free of it's grip.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/393-godjaw","name":"Godjaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar393_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"665"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-10T23:18:17-08:00","id":336797,"title":"","content":"Oooo now there's a nasty story idea: Abyssal who has had their Monstrance destroyed but their Deathlord has kept that secret and still hangs the threat of it over their head until such time as the big reveal happens and they go renegade.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1318-kindledradial","name":"kindledRadial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1318_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-11T06:21:33-08:00","id":336979,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>kindledRadial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/333352-3e-abyssals-exalted-hauntings?p=336513#post336513\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">General: The actual wording is that such charms and all necromancy spells treat the monstrance &quot;as if it were a physical extension of her body, transmitting the effects of the magic directly to her.&quot; So Pestilence-Bearing Touch still works, since if you affect one part of an exalt's body with the great contagion it <i>will</i> spread to the rest of her, for example.</div> </div> </div> </div>That is an incorrect interpretation. First, the meaning of &quot;arcane link&quot; is known. It is &quot;a physical estension of body&quot;, true, but it applies to things like cut nails, hairs etc (as well as objects with significant meaning to the target). The effect is generally dependant on the spell in question, but is not so simple as &quot;cast magic at arcane link, target gets affected&quot;.<br /> <br /> &quot;ARCANE LINKS<br /> Hair, blood, excrement and bits of flesh possess a mystic connection to the person they came from. So do favored tools, beloved dolls, well-worn clothing and other possessions, as well as relatives or lovers. Some spells require this \u201carcane link\u201d to affect their target at all. More importantly, arcane links enable some spells to affect targets at great distances, even if the spell caster<br /> doesn\u2019t know the subject\u2019s location. Most such spells require a specific arcane link, as described in the spell\u2019s text, but some spells allow for any arcane link.&quot; (White and black treatise, page 6).<br /> <br /> Second, it mentions that only <i>some</i> charms can use Monstrance as arcane link. Which ones? It is not specified... but the charm description of Screaming in Silence (abyssal communications charm) and False Heart Mien (disguise charm) do mention that they can use Monstrance that way. Which imples that every charm that lacks that information <b>cannot</b>.<br /> <br /> So, no, if you were to use Pestilence-Bearing Touch on Monstrance, the effect would be the same as if you used it on any other block of metal - <b>nothing</b>.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><i>The difference between fiction and reality? Fiction has to make sense.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/434-astralporing","name":"Astralporing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar434_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"296"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-11T07:17:48-08:00","id":336992,"title":"","content":"The important part is that the Monstrance can be used in any place where you could use a (cut-off) part of the Abyssal's body.<br /> <br /> Most spells that ask for an Arcane Link ask for &quot;at least X, or better&quot; - so, while a favourite tool might be good enough for a tracking spell, another spell might at least need a lock of hair. Some spells need actual bits of flesh.<br /> In general, a &quot;better&quot; Arcane Link can be used in place of a &quot;weaker&quot; one - so, you can replace a favourite tool or lock of hair with a bit of flesh, but not the other way around.<br /> The Monstrance here is on the same level as &quot;bit of flesh&quot;, so it can nearly always be used as an Arcane Link - it always counts as a recently cut-out piece of flesh (which is pretty much as strong as an Arcane Link can get). <br /> <br /> But, in the end, it's still just an Arcane Link.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1313-dusk-shine","name":"Dusk Shine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1313_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"256"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-11T07:32:10-08:00","id":337000,"title":"","content":"I am uncertain on that reading, although it is under a arcane link header, the fact that it says that all necromancy spells treat the monstrance as a physical extension of the abyssal body. most necromancy spells don't use arcane links, also no abyssal charms need arcane links yet it states that certain abyssal charms treat it the same. Much in the way that Unholy is listed as a header I am unconvinced that they meant the header arcane link to mean it was only that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1166-korekore","name":"korekore","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1166_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"141"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-11T08:49:20-08:00","id":337071,"title":"","content":"Also Abyssals are specifically immune to the Great Contagion and all lesser variations of it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-11T12:22:26-08:00","id":337304,"title":"","content":"CountAlucard: Ah, good save, I forgot about that.<br /> <br /> AstralPoring: First of all the words &quot;interpretation&quot; and &quot;incorrect&quot; don't belong together when we are discussing tabletop setting alterations. Second, it <i>is </i>a perfectly valid interpretation even if you do decide to ignore it in your own game. As Korekore has said, the wording of abyssal monstrances does <i>not</i> say &quot;treat a monstrance as an arcane link&quot; it <i>specifically</i> says &quot;treat as an extension of the abyssal's own body&quot; which is <i>not</i> the same thing as having a chunk of severed flesh to <i>use</i> as an arcane link, at all. The more general rule always loses out to the more specific in RPG rules-lawyering. The fact that the monstrance's description expressly states that magic targeting the monstrance &quot;transmit(s) the magic directly to (the abyssal)&quot; means that this is more than an arcane link to me, because that is <i>not</i> what an arcane link does. You can ignore that bit of rule in your game if you want, but that's not what the book is saying here.<br /> <br /> General: again I feel like we're having a good discussion but it's sort of veering off-topic, so I'm going to pose another question: if you divorce some or all abyssal characters from the Deathlords and Neverborn in terms of themes and concepts, what should be put in their place? I like the idea of abyssals as tragic heroes, hence my original post, but does anyone have something else they'd rather see abyssals become in Ex3?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1318-kindledradial","name":"kindledRadial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1318_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-11T12:27:46-08:00","id":337316,"title":"","content":"Well as the name death knight implies I have always been fond of their interpretation as champions of the dead, the ones who stand up for them to the living world which has ceased to care, who helps right their wrongs and remind the world they exist and matter. To be to the dead as the solars are to the living. Their champions, representatives, also empowering them and, much as the chosen of the sun do, manipulating and organizing them","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1166-korekore","name":"korekore","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1166_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"141"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-11T12:41:23-08:00","id":337339,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>kindledRadial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/333352-3e-abyssals-exalted-hauntings?p=337304#post337304\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Second, it <i>is </i>a perfectly valid interpretation even if you do decide to ignore it in your own game. As Korekore has said, the wording of abyssal monstrances does <i>not</i> say &quot;treat a monstrance as an arcane link&quot; it <i>specifically</i> says &quot;treat as an extension of the abyssal's own body&quot; which is <i>not</i> the same thing as having a chunk of severed flesh to <i>use</i> as an arcane link, at all. The more general rule always loses out to the more specific in RPG rules-lawyering. The fact that the monstrance's description expressly states that magic targeting the monstrance &quot;transmit(s) the magic directly to (the abyssal)&quot; means that this is more than an arcane link to me, because that is <i>not</i> what an arcane link does. You can ignore that bit of rule in your game if you want, but that's not what the book is saying here.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think that was intended. I think it was intended to be more like an arcane link and then someone didn't use the correct term of art and instead substituted a very general and easily-open-to-bad-interpretation phrasing like &quot;treat as extension of own body.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>kindledRadial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/333352-3e-abyssals-exalted-hauntings?p=336513#post336513\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">By that same token I would say things that hurt the monstrance still probably hurt you, at the very least insofar as carrying over wound penalties form being <i>on fire</i> on one part of your body.</div> </div> </div> </div>No. Jesus fucking christ, no. Any ST who uses this tortured interpretation is a total asshole who is going to any and all lengths possible to fuck you over for their own sick pleasure. Use a little common sense. Even though Abyssal crunch is terrible, you should feel bad for even implying that this is how the wording should be interpreted.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>kindledRadial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/333352-3e-abyssals-exalted-hauntings?p=337304#post337304\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">does anyone have something else they'd rather see abyssals become in Ex3?</div> </div> </div> </div>I would like &quot;champion of the dead&quot; to be a legit and unironic concept because as it stands, ghosts should fear and hate Abyssals as much as mortals do. I think scaling back the power of Deathlords and making them each a regional threat, versus each being a global threat, goes a long way to change the attitude from completely looking down on/not giving a shit about ghosts to treating them as valuable advisors at best, or valuable chattel at worst.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-11T13:11:20-08:00","id":337358,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/333352-3e-abyssals-exalted-hauntings?p=337339#post337339\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think that was intended. I think it was intended to be more like an arcane link and then someone didn't use the correct term of art and instead substituted a very general and easily-open-to-bad-interpretation phrasing like &quot;treat as extension of own body.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>It's possible, but until we see an errata on that front all we have to work with is this very punishing canon. And frankly, I think the devs knew about this popular interpretation while they wrote 2.5, and we saw <i>some</i> improvements on that front, but not on this. They could easily have said that the monstrance was <i>just</i> a normal arcane link in the 2.5 errata but they chose not to.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/333352-3e-abyssals-exalted-hauntings?p=337339#post337339\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No. Jesus fucking christ, no. Any ST who uses this tortured interpretation is a total asshole who is going to any and all lengths possible to fuck you over for their own sick pleasure. Use a little common sense. Even though Abyssal crunch is terrible, you should feel bad for even implying that this is how the wording should be interpreted.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is the point where I slowly don a pair of screaming soulsteel shades and tell you to just deal with it, sucka. In seriousness though there's wiggle room here to say different things in your own canon. Just because the monstrance counts as an extension of your body does not mean necessarily that it is hooked up to your nervous system, but you're well within rights to say that it is, also. It all depends on what you <i>want</i> to play. You may find this hard to believe but some of us <i>like</i> having a challenge when we play this game. Not everyone wants to play Super Mario with their solaroid. Some of us want the Dark Souls experience.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/333352-3e-abyssals-exalted-hauntings?p=337339#post337339\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I would like &quot;champion of the dead&quot; to be a legit and unironic concept because as it stands, ghosts should fear and hate Abyssals as much as mortals do. I think scaling back the power of Deathlords and making them each a regional threat, versus each being a global threat, goes a long way to change the attitude from completely looking down on/not giving a shit about ghosts to treating them as valuable advisors at best, or valuable chattel at worst.</div> </div> </div> </div>I can get behind what you and korekore are saying and it's always bothered me that players have to work extra hard to play this in canon because of bad setting writing (the Deathlords). I think a big scale-back is in order for them in Ex3, for sure. That said how can we represent this in mechanics? Does the abyssal charmset already allow this? Would including another mechanic, such as mitigating resonance by helping the dead, also model this idea?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1318,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1318-kindledradial","user":"kindledRadial","date":". 12-11-2014, 04:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1318-kindledradial","name":"kindledRadial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1318_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-11T14:36:25-08:00","id":337429,"title":"","content":"Mitigating resonance could be a small part but I I think charms are the best route, things like solar training charms that affect ghosts, a expansion that let's them regain motes by taking care of ghosts instead of just by eating people. Charms that let them immunize ghosts from disillusion or from reliance on their fetters, things that generally help them work with ghosts and help ghosts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1166-korekore","name":"korekore","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1166_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"141"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-11T15:05:34-08:00","id":337438,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>kindledRadial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/333352-3e-abyssals-exalted-hauntings?p=337358#post337358\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is the point where I slowly don a pair of screaming soulsteel shades and tell you to just deal with it, sucka. In seriousness though there's wiggle room here to say different things in your own canon. Just because the monstrance counts as an extension of your body does not mean necessarily that it is hooked up to your nervous system, but you're well within rights to say that it is, also. It all depends on what you <i>want</i> to play. You may find this hard to believe but some of us <i>like</i> having a challenge when we play this game. Not everyone wants to play Super Mario with their solaroid. Some of us want the Dark Souls experience.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not to get into the debate of to what extent one can pop an abyssal with charms and sorcery/necromancy using the monstrance. There is more of a precedent for the idea that damaging the monstrance doesn't actually hurt the abyssal. I mean from a logical standpoint if an attack can harm a monstrance it can harm the abyssal, but I'm speaking in the literal sense of &quot;Things which can punch holes in a tank can punch holes in people not in tanks too.&quot; Not in the sense of shooting a tank will injure the tank's crew even if they aren't in the tank.<br /> <br /> First one of the parts of a redemption path involves destroying the monstrance. I grant that no solid path for ceasing to be an abyssal was ever made, but if damage to monstrance correlated into immediate damage to the abyssal then this would not even be suggested because that step would be literal suicide. Second one of the high level abyssal charms involve the Neverborn destroying the abyssal's monstrance again this would murder the abyssal if damage were shared between the two. <br /> <br /> Also your statement about wanting the Dark Souls experience doesn't work because what you are arguing for is a being to be able to rip your character apart at will at range with no possibility of retaliation or escape. Dark Souls may have been dangerous, but I don't recall any situation that came down to &quot;X is annoyed with you. You now have only 2 hp.&quot;<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-11T16:05:17-08:00","id":337473,"title":"","content":"Nalak: Apparently you never got killed by basilisks. Or got invaded by Dark Wraiths. It's a good point about the redemption canon, though. I guess I had always sort of assumed there was some &quot;safe&quot; way to destroy the monstrance like counter-magic or even an &quot;off switch.&quot; Certainly the integrity charm that breaks your monstrance is &quot;safe&quot; insofar as the Neverborn personally handle that for you. But still, a good point.<br /> <br /> In any case my preference there is not for certain death (which is sort of how they are written) but rather for meaningful consequences. Rebelling should be scary because otherwise the decision to rebel carries no weight.The monstrance works well as a story device to justify servitude to these entities for those who <i>wish</i> to play those stories. It's the big stick to the carrot that is the liege background, that makes loyalists <i>stay</i> loyalist. I don't want it to be a pathway to instant character <i>death</i> but it should be a device for character <i>harm</i>. Not allowing the Deathlords to hurt you through your monstrance is just as silly to me as still being able to draw from your liege background after rebelling.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1318-kindledradial","name":"kindledRadial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1318_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-11T16:20:35-08:00","id":337479,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>kindledRadial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/333352-3e-abyssals-exalted-hauntings?p=337473#post337473\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I guess I had always sort of assumed there was some &quot;safe&quot; way to destroy the monstrance like counter-magic or even an &quot;off switch.&quot; Certainly the integrity charm that breaks your monstrance is &quot;safe&quot; insofar as the Neverborn personally handle that for you.</div> </div> </div> </div>Here's my view on the subject.<br /> <br /> Throwing a Monstrance into Oblivion is a method of destroying said Monstrance that is as utter and complete as is possible within the setting. Because you're basically throwing it into a black hole.<br /> <br /> It does nothing to the living Abyssal whose Exaltation is tied to that Monstrance. <br /> <br /> So, extrapolating backwards from that, why would setting that Monstrance on fire do anything to the Abyssal? It doesn't make sense. <br /> <br /> I don't want to delve into the &quot;arcane link or better&quot; argument again because I think your mind is made up and because I think the MOEP for Abyssals was a complete failure in mechanical execution. But that aside, it doesn't make any sense to me that destroying the Monstrance via Oblivion doesn't hurt you (chucking something into Oblivion, again, being the way to destroy something so spectacularly you can be assured it will never return) but hitting it with a sword would hurt you, or even provide enough sympathetic feedback so as to cause you penalties. If Damage 10 does nothing to you, why would Damage 3 do worse?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>kindledRadial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/333352-3e-abyssals-exalted-hauntings?p=337473#post337473\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not allowing the Deathlords to hurt you through your monstrance is just as silly to me as still being able to draw from your liege background after rebelling.</div> </div> </div> </div>Really depends on the nature of your rebellion, doesn't it?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-11T16:50:44-08:00","id":337528,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/333352-3e-abyssals-exalted-hauntings?p=337479#post337479\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...it doesn't make any sense to me that destroying the Monstrance via Oblivion doesn't hurt you (chucking something into Oblivion, again, being the way to destroy something so spectacularly you can be assured it will never return) but hitting it with a sword would hurt you, or even provide enough sympathetic feedback so as to cause you penalties. If Damage 10 does nothing to you, why would Damage 3 do worse?</div> </div> </div> </div>Because one of those things is just &quot;damage&quot; and one of them is &quot;damage and also the metaphysical root of all abyssal power.&quot; If you throw Captain America into a gamma radiation bath he gets cancer and dies, but if you throw in un-powered Bruce Banner he turns into the incredible Hulk and also gets a temporary stat boost. And now I've had a chance to reference cartoons, video games and comic book canon in the same thread. This has been a good day for me.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/333352-3e-abyssals-exalted-hauntings?p=337479#post337479\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Really depends on the nature of your rebellion, doesn't it?</div> </div> </div> </div><i>No</i> it super <i>doesn't!</i> Your liege rating is a mechanical representation of the fact that your Deathlord is still <i>supporting you</i>, so unless you are doing the &quot;rebelled as planned&quot; narrative previously discussed there is literally <i>no reason</i> you should still have a liege background! That's basically telling your players &quot;none of your actions will ever have consequences&quot; so I <i>really</i> hope I'm just misunderstanding you here.<br /> <br /> I reiterate: abyssal stories should be tragic. Tragedy requires sacrifice. Making the consequences of your player's actions evident is thus <i>extremely</i> important in these games. When they piss into the wind, the wind should piss on them. Handing your players a free pass to dick around and never deal with the fallout is not what we should be aiming for with abyssal narratives. Again, we <i>have this</i> already. If you take away resonance and you pull the teeth our of the monstrances and the Deathlords then <i>what is left</i> to help along that narrative?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1318,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1318-kindledradial","user":"kindledRadial","date":". 12-11-2014, 07:56 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1318-kindledradial","name":"kindledRadial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1318_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-11T16:59:01-08:00","id":337532,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>kindledRadial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/333352-3e-abyssals-exalted-hauntings?p=337473#post337473\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nalak: Apparently you never got killed by basilisks. Or got invaded by Dark Wraiths. It's a good point about the redemption canon, though. I guess I had always sort of assumed there was some &quot;safe&quot; way to destroy the monstrance like counter-magic or even an &quot;off switch.&quot; Certainly the integrity charm that breaks your monstrance is &quot;safe&quot; insofar as the Neverborn personally handle that for you. But still, a good point.</div> </div> </div> </div>No see those creatures don't really fit because one can still oppose them. The logic of Lion smashes in the face plate of your Monstrance with a hammer and it causes equivalent damage to your character doesn't match up.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>kindledRadial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/333352-3e-abyssals-exalted-hauntings?p=337473#post337473\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In any case my preference there is not for certain death (which is sort of how they are written) but rather for meaningful consequences. Rebelling should be scary because otherwise the decision to rebel carries no weight.The monstrance works well as a story device to justify servitude to these entities for those who <i>wish</i> to play those stories. It's the big stick to the carrot that is the liege background, that makes loyalists <i>stay</i> loyalist. I don't want it to be a pathway to instant character <i>death</i> but it should be a device for character <i>harm</i>. Not allowing the Deathlords to hurt you through your monstrance is just as silly to me as still being able to draw from your liege background after rebelling.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not saying you want instant death and I get that you want threat from rebellion that's fine, but if you make it too easy for the Deathlords to harm the player then it stops being the stick to the liege carrot and becomes the bomb implanted in your brain to the liege carrot.<br /> <br /> Remember though the Deathlords are still powerful skilled and will have tons of resources available to them. While I don't think 3rd will keep the scale of it from 2nd I doubt those facts will change. Doesn't take much to have your face handed out as a known anathema to all the immaculate order posts,so wyld hunts hound you and people won't associate you because you're a known monster. Abyssals can be sent to hunt you down. Squads of the undead can be sent to destroy you. I mean granted we've seen debate over what the Monstrance can do as far as spell targeting, but considering it is where your exaltation goes when you die I would guess it could be reasonably used in tracking magic and how many problems can come from the simple fact of the Deathlord being able to track you wherever you go.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-11T17:03:01-08:00","id":337535,"title":"","content":"Not sure where this fixation of tragedy came from for Abyssals. You're the dark mirrors of Solars, infused with the power of death. You are glorious and dark, you are gothic and romantic, you are beautiful and terrifying horror. Is there an element of tragedy? Yes there is, but that's isn't the focus at all. Abyssals were born from having a &quot;Vampire&quot; splat, they're inspired by Vampire, but it isn't constrained by it. Look for the reasoning and designs behind Vampires in OWoD, and why people loved to play them, and you'll find a plethora of themes that can be used for Abyssals.<br /> <br /> As for rebelling and having a liege rating. You do know you can make them lose that rating yes? If your rebellion is known to the Deathlord, you can be sure you won't have the support of the liege rating. That's what Zelbinnean means when they say &quot;the nature of your rebellion&quot; if you openly decree yourself a rebel, you won't have support, but if you are subtle about it, you can still manage it. Doing this comes with consequences and story hooks of their own, having to weight your loyalties, and being clandestine in your plans so your master doesn't discover them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/393-godjaw","name":"Godjaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar393_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"665"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-11T17:20:37-08:00","id":337571,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>kindledRadial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/333352-3e-abyssals-exalted-hauntings?p=337528#post337528\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Because one of those things is just &quot;damage&quot; and one of them is &quot;damage and also the metaphysical root of all abyssal power.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Mechanically, fire, swords, and Oblivion are the same regarding what they do to your character. Throw a Monstrance into Oblivion = no damage to Abyssal, Monstrance annihilated. Throw the Abyssal into Oblivion = Abyssal is annihilated, Exaltation separates from the destroyed body. Your argument simply doesn't hold water.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>kindledRadial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/333352-3e-abyssals-exalted-hauntings?p=337528#post337528\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><i>No</i> it super <i>doesn't!</i> Your liege rating is a mechanical representation of the fact that your Deathlord is still <i>supporting you</i>, so unless you are doing the &quot;rebelled as planned&quot; narrative previously discussed there is literally <i>no reason</i> you should still have a liege background! That's basically telling your players &quot;none of your actions will ever have consequences&quot; so I <i>really</i> hope I'm just misunderstanding you here.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you can't rebel and foment insurrection and sabotage etc. while presenting a face of loyalty, you're not thinking very creatively.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>kindledRadial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/333352-3e-abyssals-exalted-hauntings?p=337528#post337528\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I reiterate: abyssal stories should be tragic. Tragedy requires sacrifice . . . Again, we <i>have this</i> already. If you take away resonance and you pull the teeth our of the monstrances and the Deathlords then <i>what is left</i> to help along that narrative?</div> </div> </div> </div>I dunno where you get the tragedy thing. At any rate, it's your personal preference that Abyssal stories be tragic. Tragic heroism is not a core theme of every Abyssal in the same way that &quot;wields the power of death and decay, both figuratively and literally&quot; is.<br /> <br /> And the 1e/2e Abyssal narrative has always come across as an extremely OWoD-esque narrative with its hit-you-over-the-head punishment mechanics and elder-younger power dynamics, not an Exalted narrative.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>kindledRadial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/333352-3e-abyssals-exalted-hauntings?p=337528#post337528\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Making the consequences of your player's actions evident is thus <i>extremely</i> important in these games. When they piss into the wind, the wind should piss on them. Handing your players a free pass to dick around and never deal with the fallout is not what we should be aiming for with abyssal narratives.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Actions have consequences&quot; is not a uniquely Abyssal splat theme; it's a core theme of the entire Exalted game line and all splats within it. And it's not a theme that should apply extra-hard to Abyssals for no reason.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-11T17:45:42-08:00","id":337589,"title":"","content":"Again, seeing a lot of the same comments so I'm going to reply in general:<br /> <br /> The Deathlords are a huge problem for the abyssals <i>as characters</i> in Ex2 that needs to get addressed in Ex3. Many of the problems people are commenting on vis-a-vis the monstrance are problems with the Deathlords and their <i>use</i> of the monstrances rather than the monstrances themselves. And yes, you could remove both entirely and lose nothing from the narrative except one more hardship the abyssals suffer in canon, which <i>seems </i>to be what a lot of people want: an abyssal game where everything is easy. This perplexes me.<br /> <br /> Why do any of you <i>play</i> abyssals? <i>Do</i> you play abyssals? What is the draw for you?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1318-kindledradial","name":"kindledRadial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1318_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-11T18:22:52-08:00","id":337605,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>kindledRadial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/333352-3e-abyssals-exalted-hauntings?p=337589#post337589\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Again, seeing a lot of the same comments so I'm going to reply in general:<br /> <br /> The Deathlords are a huge problem for the abyssals <i>as characters</i> in Ex2 that needs to get addressed in Ex3. Many of the problems people are commenting on vis-a-vis the monstrance are problems with the Deathlords and their <i>use</i> of the monstrances rather than the monstrances themselves. And yes, you could remove both entirely and lose nothing from the narrative except one more hardship the abyssals suffer in canon, which <i>seems </i>to be what a lot of people want: an abyssal game where everything is easy. This perplexes me.<br /> <br /> Why do any of you <i>play</i> abyssals? <i>Do</i> you play abyssals? What is the draw for you?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I love the anti-hero. Between a genuine hero and a right bastard with his heart in the right place i'd take the latter. I'd take Spawn over Superman anyday. I also love gothic literature and gothic imagery. Dark passions and romance contrasted with death. I'm greatly entertained by tragedies (the plays) and dark comedy.<br /> <br /> I've played a personally tragic Abyssal whose love died, and he almost did but he Exalted. He was compelled to the Underworld in search of his lost love, and when he found her he had her forged into a Soulsteel blade, crimson like blood with the image of a dancing lover reflected in the blade, in anguish and excasty. He fought for lovers and lost loves, and found himself superficially in the service of the Lover Clad in a Raiment of Tears. There he learned to manipulate love as a tool, and his sword burned bright with jealousy striking down foes in hopes to win his love again. He was always more of a lover than a fighter, very superficial with his love, but always kept his daiklaive close.<br /> <br /> I also played a total monster who was more of a protector than a killer, but only as a lure for danger. Once a mortal stood up against a Dynast to protect another, and was run through with the daiklaive. At that moment the mortal exploded with a dark and deathly anima, and wrenched the blade from his chest, and slew the surprised Dynast who was not the fighter they boasted to be with their own weapon. When all was done, he returned the blade to it's new sheath, within his chest. The person he was protecting became like a thrall, friend, and lure to him, terrified and loyal. He was contacted by the Princess Magnificent who sought others like him to help her protect the people of the south from the machinations of the Lion. He agreed if only to find more victims. He's a shadow on the sands of the South, a sadistic avenger whose path often walks with travelling caravans. <br /> <br /> Those are two I can remember off the top of my head.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/393-godjaw","name":"Godjaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar393_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"665"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-11T18:32:25-08:00","id":337609,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>kindledRadial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/333352-3e-abyssals-exalted-hauntings?p=337589#post337589\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Again, seeing a lot of the same comments so I'm going to reply in general:<br /> <br /> The Deathlords are a huge problem for the abyssals <i>as characters</i> in Ex2 that needs to get addressed in Ex3. Many of the problems people are commenting on vis-a-vis the monstrance are problems with the Deathlords and their <i>use</i> of the monstrances rather than the monstrances themselves. And yes, you could remove both entirely and lose nothing from the narrative except one more hardship the abyssals suffer in canon, which <i>seems </i>to be what a lot of people want: an abyssal game where everything is easy. This perplexes me.<br /> <br /> Why do any of you <i>play</i> abyssals? <i>Do</i> you play abyssals? What is the draw for you?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well to be fair you get keep trying to push the same case your going to get the same responses. From what I've gathered you don't just want abyssals to have it hard you want everything to pummel the abyssals that they should be entirely defined and ruled by tragedy. Your case for abyssals is that they would be better if they were all the whinny &quot;my life sucks and everything I do ends up making my life worse&quot; situation that makes me have no interest in the Wraith line. No the issue with the Monstrance aren't the Deathlords and their use its that you keep making a case that the existence of the Monstrance means the Deathlords should be able to quickly and easily maim if not destroy any Abyssal who they even suspect of being disloyal to them. You keep arguing that if the Abyssals aren't constantly being humilated and punished for everything up to and including continuing to exist (to bring up your idea that resonance should punish an abyssal for not finishing the goal and dying) then you are playing them wrong.<br /> <br /> Abyssals are the closest to death incarnate of any 2nd edition splat. You focus on tragedy, but I've had a character who took the black exaltation as an excuse to really live because he'd basically died once before. Oh he picked up the resonance ,you can only save so many lives without killing anything before it happens you know, but that was a consequence of the action. I had a player who just hunted slave rings and massacred them with the excuse being that he died in a slaver raid and had a rather large grudge against it. I've seen another who used the fact that abyssals are supposedly immortal unless killed as an excuse to start crazy plans like seeing if she couldn't set off a chain of events that left a city in ashes and started with planting a shrub in between attempting to master void circle necromancy and solar circle sorcery. (The last bit was her character goal since 2nd had that annoying needs an epic motivation thing, so she went with learn solar sorcery.)<br /> <br /> Also had a brief game where the abyssal and infernal in the party realized their job of spreading chaos and death was made much easier by just talking the Solar out of obviously suicidal plans and keeping people from killing him. That one though was silly, but fun was had.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-11T18:58:28-08:00","id":337627,"title":"","content":"The main difference I see between your and <i>my</i> opinion is where these hardships and difficulties should come from. <br /> <br /> I like Abyssals who have huge trouble living in the living world and helping people, because their abilities are ill-suited to help and prone to go out of control. <br /> <br /> Adding &quot;Oh, and Deathlords can kill you any time, any place&quot; is just over the top and distracting. I'd prefer if the Abyssal theme was &quot;All you have is a hammer, but the problem is a broken vase&quot;, not &quot;All you have is a hammer, and you wear an electroshock collar. Screw the vase, you have bigger problems.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1313-dusk-shine","name":"Dusk Shine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1313_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"256"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-11T19:23:45-08:00","id":337634,"title":"","content":"On monstrances: I think maybe my playing devil's advocate resulted in some misunderstandings. I <i>do</i> think the monstrances gave too much power to NPCs with regards to PCs, and I would not at all mind them actually being down graded into <i>just</i> arcane links that guarantee perfect tracking. They aren't at present though, is what I am saying.<br /> <br /> Godjaw: I like these character ideas and I'd play either one of them, myself. We might be pursuing different trends, but at least now I see where you are coming from. Is the draw in these cases that your characters are doing good things for the &quot;wrong&quot; reasons? How is this different from your experience playing a solar, who's great curse also makes them act selfishly in the pursuit of &quot;good&quot; intentions? If your character exalted in my proposed canon with a black exaltation that kept them &quot;on track&quot; in their original goals what would that take away or add, if anything?<br /> <br /> Nalak: These examples may not be the best ones in your defense since they seem to support the Ex2 mentality of &quot;abyssals are evil nihilists who kill for fun and profit.&quot; How would you play an abyssal that wasn't a proponent of Oblivion? Or a pacifist? Is that even a thing you want to be <i>able</i> to do? Could you put into words, please, what you want to do most when you make an abyssal?<br /> <br /> Dusk Shine: I also like that abyssals are more of the Underworld than of their native Creation, and that conflict has some good story hooks. I'm a bit iffy on this whole &quot;hammer-vase&quot; analogy though, since that immediately makes me think of the Ex2 abyssal charmset and how the only thing it did waskill things. I never did like this and I always will find it very limiting during character gen. I'd rather that, like the Infernal charmsets, the abyssal charms allowed you to accomplish <i>any</i> feat but in your own gothic way, such as peaceably solving inter-personal discord by suppressing or erasing intimacies. The fact that Ex2 abyssal charms <i>always</i> racked up a body count got super old to me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1318,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1318-kindledradial","user":"kindledRadial","date":". 12-11-2014, 11:05 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1318-kindledradial","name":"kindledRadial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1318_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-11T19:52:37-08:00","id":337657,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>kindledRadial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/333352-3e-abyssals-exalted-hauntings?p=337634#post337634\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Godjaw: I like these character ideas and I'd play either one of them, myself. We might be pursuing different trends, but at least now I see where you are coming from. Is the draw in these cases that your characters are doing good things for the &quot;wrong&quot; reasons? How is this different from your experience playing a solar, who's great curse also makes them act selfishly in the pursuit of &quot;good&quot; intentions? If your character exalted in my proposed canon with a black exaltation that kept them &quot;on track&quot; in their original goals what would that take away or add, if anything?</div> </div> </div> </div>The difference for me is aesthetic and theme from Solars. Could I play a dickish Superman vibrant with the power of the Sun? Sure, but i'd rather play an anti-hero who uses the very powers of death and the damned. Tormented haunting ghosts, swirling black abysses, stigmata doom and death. A power so blasphemous and profane to life and light it burns the flesh when it emerges, causing the caste mark to leak blood. They are damned, and I freaking love it. Just as glorious as the Solar and it's shining beacon, but dark, black, deathly. They're fucking metal.<br /> <br /> As for your canon, both of them didn't have Monstrances, as one was very much superficially using the Lover to learn to manipulate love, while the other only agreed to help the Princess so he could lure in more victims. I imagine with Monstrances they would be tied much more strongly to the Deathlords, forgoing some of their independence in service to their masters. Both were incredibly independent characters, one willingly went into the Underworld himself to find the ghost of his lover, and to be with her forever had a masterful ghost smith soulforge her into a daiklaive. It loses some of it's mystery and impact to me if say the Lover told him where to go to find her, and provided the smith to make the daiklaive.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Saw your edited post. How can we represent that in game terms? Give them cool damned, dark, and deathly powers that are just as glorious as Solar powers. Also options and cool things to do in those scopes. Evoking those things comes naturally then. I also had an idea that resonance isn't the punishment of the Neverborn, but a consequence of the Abyssal power. Restoring essence in Creation causes it, supplanting Creation's essence with deathly essence. This kills and corrupts, but the Abyssal can control it, his is very thematic for me, drawing in essence from blood, or the green life around them, or the softness of a child or lover.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":393,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/393-godjaw","user":"Godjaw","date":". 12-11-2014, 11:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/393-godjaw","name":"Godjaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar393_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"665"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-11T20:30:46-08:00","id":337674,"title":"","content":"General: sorry if anyone else made posts before my edits, I thought I was quick but not quick enough I guess.<br /> <br /> Godjaw: definitely feeling you on the &quot;most metal exalt&quot; vibe, I'll try and keep that in mind so none of my ideas get in your way there. I would say here again as I did for Dusk Shine that this was poorly handled in Ex2, though, with every single charm resulting in collateral damage ala Metalocalypse which got in the way of <i>other</i> story concepts. While I definitely want you to be <i>able</i> to play Nathan Explosion, the fact that <i>every </i>performance spec became him eventually was annoying to me.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Also shards heavily implied that resonance <i>does</i> come from the abyssal exaltation itself, so you get no argument from me on that point. That's actually why I wanted to pursue this idea of resonance tied to your character's motivation, rather than someone else's.<br /> <br /> Also, because I again probably didn't do a very good job explaining myself here, I disliked how Resonance would arbitrarily hurt you for preserving life in Ex2. That's a <i>very </i>heavy-handed limiter to put on an entire splat and I sincerely hope we nix it in Ex3 such that not <i>every </i>good and decent act is punishable by unsoakable health level loss. Did anyone actually <i>like</i> that?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1318,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1318-kindledradial","user":"kindledRadial","date":". 12-11-2014, 11:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1318-kindledradial","name":"kindledRadial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1318_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-11T21:05:15-08:00","id":337685,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>kindledRadial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/333352-3e-abyssals-exalted-hauntings?p=337674#post337674\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, because I again probably didn't do a very good job explaining myself here, I disliked how Resonance would arbitrarily hurt you for preserving life in Ex2. That's a <i>very </i>heavy-handed limiter to put on an entire splat and I sincerely hope we nix it in Ex3 such that not <i>every </i>good and decent act is punishable by unsoakable health level loss. Did anyone actually <i>like</i> that?</div> </div> </div> </div>Everything in Exalted has a fan somewhere, even Ma-ha-sushi's rape camp and Raski being an drooling mouth-breathing idiot, hell, there are even people who like the first two chapters of MoEP: Infernal.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The no.1 fan of Demetheus. I also draw <a href=\"https://probably-unreliable.tumblr.com/tagged/Jenart\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted</a> things and is looking for commission works ~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","name":"Jen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar298_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-11T21:17:19-08:00","id":337689,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/333352-3e-abyssals-exalted-hauntings?p=337685#post337685\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Everything in Exalted has a fan somewhere, even Ma-ha-sushi's rape camp and Raski being an drooling mouth-breathing idiot, hell, there are even people who like the first two chapters of MoEP: Infernal.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>RE: the second Infernals chapter, its problems manifest entirely as the background of a single character and the existence of mortal akuma (as akuma become capable of using Yozi Charms and that works for Exalted but holy shit not for mortals or God-Blooded). Taking the Urge mechanic into account to make those characters playable or at least ST-manageable, it's a cut above the 1e akuma material and certainly better than the God-Blooded section of the Scroll of Heroes, particularly regarding Demon-Blooded (&quot;area of sin&quot; for Essence recovery woo woo!). But where it's bad, it gets sucked down into the abyss of its immediate predecessor chapter.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-11T21:22:55-08:00","id":337691,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/333352-3e-abyssals-exalted-hauntings?p=337685#post337685\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Everything in Exalted has a fan somewhere, even Ma-ha-sushi's rape camp and Raski being an drooling mouth-breathing idiot, hell, there are even people who like the first two chapters of MoEP: Infernal.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Infernal fans always just ignore those chapters and it's a beautiful thing but I wonder why I've never been able to do that for MoEP: Abyssals? I very much <i>want</i> to ignore the Deathlords but I feel like that's cheating...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1318-kindledradial","name":"kindledRadial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1318_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-11T21:34:09-08:00","id":337694,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>kindledRadial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/333352-3e-abyssals-exalted-hauntings?p=337691#post337691\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Infernal fans always just ignore those chapters and it's a beautiful thing but I wonder why I've never been able to do that for MoEP: Abyssals? I very much <i>want</i> to ignore the Deathlords but I feel like that's cheating...</div> </div> </div> </div>Because the stuff in Infernals is much less core to the GSPs' overall portrayal and even themes than the equivalent stuff in Abyssals is.<br /> <br /> Lillun existing as a thing is fine as is the notion of a sort of living Monstrance, it's her depiction and backstory and <i>that fucking comic</i> that are wholly disgusting. The Yozis celebrating every new GSP who comes to Malfeas with a Carnival/Mardi Gras is fine, it's the forced-rape depiction of the new GSP that is odious. Etc. The Yozis are portrayed as relatively distant masters who allow a relatively loose leash and only play centrally when the GSPs are actually in Malfeas. The Reclamation is really pretty awful but that's just one piece of the puzzle.<br /> <br /> By contrast, the Deathlord relationship is quite central to the Abyssal narrative, which is why rebellion/Redemption is such a forced thing for them, versus for GSPs it's an option (and the best option long-term) but pushed a whole lot less. Part of this is because the Yozis are in Malfeas and stuck there, while the GSPs are supposed to spend most of their time in Creation; their overlords are effectively locked away and can be ignored with relative safety. Abyssals and Deathlords however both operate in the Underworld and Creation, and the Deathlords aren't imprisoned or at a real disadvantage when it comes to curtailing undesirable behavior as the Yozis are.<br /> <br /> The actual Yozis are really less relevant in a day-to-day way to GSPs than Deathlords are to Abyssals, because Deathlords/Abyssals really really really want to play up a Camarilla-style sire/childe relationship on a bigger scale.<br /> <br /> Also I think that the Yozi stuff we got involved much better statblocks and mechanical assumptions (even if I personally think that statting Deathlords and Yozis at all is stupid), and of course the Deathlords by RAW are beyond all reasonable scope of power for what they have (not) accomplished.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":3420,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","user":"Zelbinnean","date":". 12-12-2014, 12:36 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-11T21:45:53-08:00","id":337739,"title":"","content":"Zelninneam: Huh. That is actually the best argument I've yet heard for taking away the monstrance as it exists currently in canon. Taking away a Deathlord's ability to &quot;check-in&quot; as a reflexive action any time they feel like and renew those compulsion/servitude effects <i>would</i> be pretty damn liberating to the death knight narrative. I'd still like them to address the fact that every death knight in canon has to get brain-raped by the Neverborn at some point as part of their initiation, and of course something, anything to stop your Deathlord from Necromancy-summoning themselves to your exact location to gank you in person. There's a reason most of my characters have had a negative intimacy towards mirrors.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1318-kindledradial","name":"kindledRadial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1318_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-11T23:59:18-08:00","id":337832,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>kindledRadial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/333352-3e-abyssals-exalted-hauntings?p=337634#post337634\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nalak: These examples may not be the best ones in your defense since they seem to support the Ex2 mentality of &quot;abyssals are evil nihilists who kill for fun and profit.&quot; How would you play an abyssal that wasn't a proponent of Oblivion? Or a pacifist? Is that even a thing you want to be <i>able</i> to do? Could you put into words, please, what you want to do most when you make an abyssal?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well to be fair murdering for fun and profit crops up in basically every splat and is tricky standpoint to move away from when your group for exalted is also your dnd group.<br /> <br /> Pacifists don't generally work in our games we don't have anything against it just none of our group finds the idea of being completely refusing to fight very fun, so nobody plays it. You'll get characters who prefer to find other options of course, but if it comes down to it the only times the party isn't willing to throw down is when they think the enemy will just destroy them.<br /> <br /> Actually the characters worked pretty well. I mean let's be fair slaughtering bandits and slavers helps people just not in the same way that a doctor does or converting those criminals to guards or something. So the one in it for the hell of it didn't care about Oblivion and would just do things based on his own opinions with information from effort and potential backlash. The one who was out for killing slavers he just considered them a blight on the world that had it coming. It wasn't a case of there is no point to anything more of &quot;these people are scum and don't deserve to live.&quot; Essentially the more psychotic avenger type evil being subjective.<br /> <br /> I got nothing on the caster that was just the kind of person her player wanted to play and no one was made uncomfortable by it,so it went through.<br /> <br /> The other two really operated on the idea that the solar was a psychopath and would cause death and destruction regardless of any actions by them. (The solar tended to try and set off minor wyld hunts so he could kill them. If not direct attacks on imperial bases.) Their logic was if they kept this solar alive they could do use him as a smokescreen for pursuing their own activities with the claim of &quot;So long as he thinks we're his allies, and not all that bad, we can manipulate him to do our job with less risks and we get to reinforce the 'Solars are monsters' view in the world too.&quot; So they got to use the Malice ,the solar, being a psycho to justify why they would do things that weren't directly feeding their faction goals.<br /> <br /> As for what we do when we play we make use of the death aspect. Usually their death informs the character in some way that was kind of important. It really varied based on what the individual wanted to do with the character. I mean I've had one player who literally played an abyssal because they wanted a justifiable excuse for blood drinking. Frankly I've had at least one abyssal character who worked the mentor angle on the grounds that he knows failure better than others because of the circumstances of his exaltation. (He got himself killed attempting heroics and got to see the impact of his failure on the event.) I'm the ST though, so mentors and informants tend to be the more likely characters to be recurring you know.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-12T09:21:15-08:00","id":338099,"title":"","content":"Nalak: it kind of sounds like you're providing the DnD experience for your players, in which case it really doesn't matter what you play. It sounds also like at least one of your abyssals pretty much just ignored his/her resonance and connection to the Deathlords and Oblivion, so again you're losing a lot of the meat there. Was there any functional difference between the solar, infernal and abyssal that you noticed in play or was it just that your party all wanted to be different things? In general, what distinction do the abyssals have that makes <i>you</i> want to play one?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1318-kindledradial","name":"kindledRadial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1318_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-12T09:45:47-08:00","id":338111,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>kindledRadial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/333352-3e-abyssals-exalted-hauntings?p=338099#post338099\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nalak: it kind of sounds like you're providing the DnD experience for your players, in which case it really doesn't matter what you play. It sounds also like at least one of your abyssals pretty much just ignored his/her resonance and connection to the Deathlords and Oblivion, so again you're losing a lot of the meat there. Was there any functional difference between the solar, infernal and abyssal that you noticed in play or was it just that your party all wanted to be different things? In general, what distinction do the abyssals have that makes <i>you</i> want to play one?</div> </div> </div> </div>They focused on avoiding resonance where they could. If they don't do anything to trigger resonance then I can't really hit them with resonance. I mean a basic thing for them was the faction goal is kill all things that one of them decided he would prioritize the destruction of slavers meant he was still going along with faction goals. So in a hypothetical scenario a town is under attack by bandits,slavers, monsters, you know things that aren't the forces of oblivion. PC goes in and decides to destroy the attackers, even though doing so saves the lives of the towns folk that isn't a resonance triggering effect since the method chosen was slaughter. I can't very well throw resonance at a player for no reason because then they get peeved and people aren't having fun. As for the Deathlords well the PCs were all new exalts with about a year under their belts they had been given a job to do for their boss, but otherwise the Deathlords felt the PCs were just insignificant tools not like they need micromanaging. As for the oblivion connection well there's not a whole lot to be done in regards to having an indirect connection to a blackhole.<br /> <br /> As I said previously the Abyssals are the dead their characters are the ones that have a great versatility in just that fact and how that based for them. Did your character die failing, die to betrayal, die randomly, die alone, die with others, die a hero? They accepted an extended life in exchange for power and service do they regret this, are they ok with this, do they think it was right, do they give a crap about it, hell are they trying to get an old friend to exalt abyssal too? I'm the storyteller I play characters, so what kind of person I am allowed to play matters and there is a lot of versatility in the kind of character that is justified in their backstory including the phrase &quot;I think it went wrong once I started to be able to look through my chest and see behind me.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-12T10:12:21-08:00","id":338131,"title":"","content":"Nalak: yeah if the only thing your party wants to do is have fun and spread some mayhem then they are naturally going to resent you for putting <i>any</i> restraints on them including the Great Curse and/or resonance. That doesn't mean these are bad mechanics in <i>general</i>, just for your party. Honestly I think you'd be better off just ignoring such mechanics in your game in favor of &quot;Grand Theft Yeddim&quot; rules where none of the power players work against you and the Wyld Hunt is comically inept. The majority of canon exalted is not set up in such a way as to support this playstyle of &quot;no consequences&quot; and I really don't think it should be.<br /> <br /> Death and second life are a major theme for abyssals, which is one of the reasons I'd like them to have more ghost-like mechanics such as those proposed. I don't think that the &quot;you only live twice&quot; mechanic is enough to separate them from other splats by itself, though. Most exalts have near-death experiences as part of their backstories; as mentioned previously most Dawns would have died if not for their timely exaltation. The question becomes how do you keep this theme fresh? That's why so much of the abyssal charmset is death-focused: they want you constantly thinking grim thoughts. So I'd say that what you like about abyssals is preserved in their charmset, which I'm not proposing to change except to add more goals besides &quot;kill that guy.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1318,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1318-kindledradial","user":"kindledRadial","date":". 12-12-2014, 02:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1318-kindledradial","name":"kindledRadial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1318_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-12T10:29:06-08:00","id":338139,"title":"","content":"I'm rather certain Abyssals aren't actually dead, but they Exalt at the cusp of death, preventing it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/393-godjaw","name":"Godjaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar393_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"665"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-12T10:49:21-08:00","id":338173,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Godjaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/333352-3e-abyssals-exalted-hauntings?p=338139#post338139\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm rather certain Abyssals aren't actually dead, but they Exalt at the cusp of death, preventing it.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is true.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-12T11:07:50-08:00","id":338181,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Godjaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/333352-3e-abyssals-exalted-hauntings?p=338139#post338139\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm rather certain Abyssals aren't actually dead, but they Exalt at the cusp of death, preventing it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah but with the whole &quot;grim specter offering you a choice&quot; thing they really play up that angle more than other exaltations. Like they don't die <i>technically</i> but the fact that they almost did is much more central to their concept. If nothing else it makes their canonical servitude to the Deathlords that much more bitter since they &quot;chose&quot; that life, technically.<br /> <br /> I've always wanted to play with that idea more, though. Again it kind of just feels like one more way they shackled abyssal concepts to the Deathlords in Ex2. The idea that either abyssals might have <i>actually</i> died or at least gone through all the essential steps before exalting, and that the nature of their death might determine what kind of exalt they become as with ghosts, were concepts I tried to work into my proposed canon.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1318-kindledradial","name":"kindledRadial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1318_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-12T13:17:35-08:00","id":338344,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>kindledRadial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/333352-3e-abyssals-exalted-hauntings?p=338131#post338131\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nalak: yeah if the only thing your party wants to do is have fun and spread some mayhem then they are naturally going to resent you for putting <i>any</i> restraints on them including the Great Curse and/or resonance. That doesn't mean these are bad mechanics in <i>general</i>, just for your party. Honestly I think you'd be better off just ignoring such mechanics in your game in favor of &quot;Grand Theft Yeddim&quot; rules where none of the power players work against you and the Wyld Hunt is comically inept. The majority of canon exalted is not set up in such a way as to support this playstyle of &quot;no consequences&quot; and I really don't think it should be.</div> </div> </div> </div> See here we have your dismissal again anything that isn't the universe pummeling an abyssal is GTY according to you. It is not a case of not wanting restrictions they view avoiding the penalty of limit, torment,and resonance as part of the challenge of playing the game. There are always threats and there are risks, granted these vary based on risk because lets be fair the danger an exalt is in when fighting a group of rhaksha is significantly more than physical and extreme then that of a debate in a bar regarding what beverage is best. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>kindledRadial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/333352-3e-abyssals-exalted-hauntings?p=338131#post338131\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Death and second life are a major theme for abyssals, which is one of the reasons I'd like them to have more ghost-like mechanics such as those proposed. I don't think that the &quot;you only live twice&quot; mechanic is enough to separate them from other splats by itself, though. Most exalts have near-death experiences as part of their backstories; as mentioned previously most Dawns would have died if not for their timely exaltation. The question becomes how do you keep this theme fresh? That's why so much of the abyssal charmset is death-focused: they want you constantly thinking grim thoughts. So I'd say that what you like about abyssals is preserved in their charmset, which I'm not proposing to change except to add more goals besides &quot;kill that guy.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>See I view it as different than those. As you put it many a Dawn would have died if their exaltation didn't happen, but the exaltation allowed them to live. The thing is for an abyssal the only reason they aren't dead is because they took the offer a Dawn caste doesn't get the option to refuse an exaltation. To put it another way one origin for The Bull of The North is that he had gone out to die his exaltation prevented his death. That he just became empowered plays up how he responds to it differently then if he had been offered the power. I mean a man in the same situation who is offered an abyssal exaltation probably won't take it because his goal is to die, but what does it say about the one who does? How does that one respond to the knowledge that when they sought their death a chance to live had been offered and they took it? <br /> As for keeping the theme fresh well you don't play a theme those are just things that go with the character you pick and how important a theme is will vary for each.<br /> <br /> @Godjaw Yeah I know they don't technically die, but considering the nature of the moment of second breath and the new home territory being the underworld its fair game to have it called &quot;the part where I died,&quot; as opposed to &quot;second breath,&quot; though &quot;when I exalted,&quot; is always a valid descriptor if you're an exalt.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-12T13:59:16-08:00","id":338375,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>kindledRadial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/333352-3e-abyssals-exalted-hauntings?p=338181#post338181\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah but with the whole &quot;grim specter offering you a choice&quot; thing they really play up that angle more than other exaltations. Like they don't die <i>technically</i> but the fact that they almost did is much more central to their concept. If nothing else it makes their canonical servitude to the Deathlords that much more bitter since they &quot;chose&quot; that life, technically.. . . Again it kind of just feels like one more way they shackled abyssal concepts to the Deathlords in Ex2.</div> </div> </div> </div>This was not new in 2e. This goes back to 1e. This has been the Abyssal narrative since the very beginning.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-12T16:42:29-08:00","id":338560,"title":"","content":"Nalak: if the only thing your players want to do with the Great Curse and resonance is avoid it, then you should just take that out of your game. Same with the Deathlords, and monstrances, and the Wyld Hunt and all that other stuff that breeds extra challenge. These things exist to produce stories, but they have to be engaged with in order to do that. If your <i>players</i> would rather just ignore them then let them. But again, this does not make these bad devices.<br /> <br /> Some (but not all) of the challenges these devices pose produce good stories. Having your Deathlord track you infallibly through glade and thicket with the burning eye of Sauron is a good story. Having a tragic hero who wants to help but is limited in their ability to not set the town hall on fire is also a good story. My only complaint is that at present every abyssal is forced into these narratives and I'd like options expanded. But if your argument is that these things shouldn't be in Exalted <i>at all </i>because they makes your character's life <i>hard</i>, then I adamantly disagree.<br /> <br /> Zelbinnean: is this an argument in favor of the current canon or just an observation?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1318-kindledradial","name":"kindledRadial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1318_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-12T17:03:30-08:00","id":338565,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>kindledRadial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/333352-3e-abyssals-exalted-hauntings?p=338560#post338560\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But if your argument is that these things shouldn't be in Exalted <i>at all </i>because they makes your character's life <i>hard</i>, then I adamantly disagree.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nobody in this thread, <i>nobody</i>, has said that actions should not have consequences. <br /> <br /> And honestly...have you ever played GTA? Because there are consequences for actions in GTA, there are also built-in easy-resolutions (which there aren't in Exalted, aside from &quot;kill, outwit, or convince your foes to stop bothering you.&quot; I don't know where you get the idea that a gonzo Grand Theft Yeddim type game is going to be very consequence-free. <br /> <br /> Also just because players want to avoid menace mechanics does not mean to remove them. If they're choosing to play things safe, that's their prerogative; it doesn't mean you don't enforce the menace when they slip up. You seem to have very particular opinions about so-called consequence free games that I MUST assume are anecdotal to you because they share nothing with my decade-plus of Exalted play experience or the apparent experience of many others on this forum.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>kindledRadial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/333352-3e-abyssals-exalted-hauntings?p=338560#post338560\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Zelbinnean: is this an argument in favor of the current canon or just an observation?</div> </div> </div> </div>An observation. You seemed to be presenting it like it was a New Thing in 2e, which it wasn't. Just that in 1e, the Deathlords were not mechanically defined as being so OP. I don't think you can read anybody in here as endorsing the RAW of 2e.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-12T17:21:13-08:00","id":338573,"title":"","content":"Zelbinnean: I <i>assumed</i> no one was based on how the thread had proceeded but honestly it's very hard to <i>tell</i> when everyone is shouting what they <i>don't</i> believe should be done at the top of their lungs and no one is putting forward what they think <i>should be done. </i>I have never said that resonance or monstrances or the Deathlords work well as they are in canon, which seems to be everyone's assumption of my meaning. I'd greatly appreciate it if everyone still participating in this conversation would say, in certain terms, what <i>they</i> think should be done with resonance, the Deathlords and monstrances before we continue because just defending our opinions round-robin style is obviously going nowhere.<br /> <br /> ALSO I still want to discuss my original thread question of &quot;would tying resonance eruptions to abyssal motivation rather than an NPC be fun for people, and/or better than what we have.&quot; So if people could start relating their comments back to that question I'd greatly appreciate it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1318-kindledradial","name":"kindledRadial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1318_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-12T18:07:48-08:00","id":338591,"title":"","content":"Well for deathlord I am fine with them being powerful ghosts, up to 3rd circle demon tier of power with themes appropriate to each and limited as appropriate to the nature of their state so passions and a mindset of the dead. <br /> For the monstrice I like it as a arcane link but I also like more to e capable through links and defenses specifically against them so it works but there are charms you can get so it's just at best a tracker and of course I would like a few more charm routes that shatter it associated with character directions. <br /> For resonance I honestly am fine with resonance in shards. Maybe some small tweaks for the stewards of the dead concept.<br /> As far as tying it to your motivation or how you exalted I actually prefer it as a upwelling from oblivion, a expression of what empowers you being a shard of oblivion which wished to see all that is become nothingness.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1166-korekore","name":"korekore","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1166_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"141"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-12T18:58:37-08:00","id":338617,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>kindledRadial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/333352-3e-abyssals-exalted-hauntings?p=338560#post338560\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nalak: if the only thing your players want to do with the Great Curse and resonance is avoid it, then you should just take that out of your game. Same with the Deathlords, and monstrances, and the Wyld Hunt and all that other stuff that breeds extra challenge. These things exist to produce stories, but they have to be engaged with in order to do that. If your <i>players</i> would rather just ignore them then let them. But again, this does not make these bad devices.</div> </div> </div> </div>Where the heck are you getting an asinine idea like that. There is no fun if there is no chance of failure. They work to avoid those things hitting them this does not mean that they don't want them in the game. They exist to create challenge yes, but the logic you espouse is that unless they are constantly being beaten with them they don't count and that is absurd. There is challenge in trying to do your own thing while avoiding the wrath of those that disagree with you.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>kindledRadial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/333352-3e-abyssals-exalted-hauntings?p=338560#post338560\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Some (but not all) of the challenges these devices pose produce good stories. Having your Deathlord track you infallibly through glade and thicket with the burning eye of Sauron is a good story. Having a tragic hero who wants to help but is limited in their ability to not set the town hall on fire is also a good story. My only complaint is that at present every abyssal is forced into these narratives and I'd like options expanded. But if your argument is that these things shouldn't be in Exalted <i>at all </i>because they makes your character's life <i>hard</i>, then I adamantly disagree.</div> </div> </div> </div>Except that isn't what you've been saying. You haven't been saying Deathlords can track you if they want so going renegade is risky, or that resonance makes being a hero harder. You've been saying Deathlords should spend all their time micromanaging their Abyssals and that the slightest thing an abyssal does that annoys the Deathlord should result in the Abyssal being maimed or killed by the Deathlord without any chance of retaliation or resistance. You haven't been arguing that resonance was should be less limiting you've been arguing that it should be leveled at every possible instance to ruin the Abyssal. You claim that anything that isn't the Abyssal being absolutely wrecked, miserable, and useless mourning how the universe hates them is not a good thing and that the people should just play GTY.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-12T19:19:19-08:00","id":338628,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>kindledRadial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/333352-3e-abyssals-exalted-hauntings?p=338573#post338573\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd greatly appreciate it if everyone still participating in this conversation would say, in certain terms, what <i>they</i> think should be done with resonance, the Deathlords and monstrances before we continue because just defending our opinions round-robin style is obviously going nowhere.</div> </div> </div> </div>Resonance: get rid of it as a choke chain that triggers off of behavior that some loser Neverborn NPC (who should be even further in the background than it already is) doesn't like, especially if said behavior ultimately serves their goals (forming emotional attachments you plan to break in order to cause despair, for example).<br /> <br /> Give it a carrot aspect as well as a stick. Pure-stick is much more appropriate for WoD than Exalted: in Exalted, there is <i>usually</i> some trade-off, some bennie that you get in exchange for your inconvenience.<br /> <br /> I also would not want it to be a purely self-inflicted wound or a &quot;punishment&quot; the Abyssals subconsciously levy on themselves. The Great Curse/Limit Break actual mechanics have been pretty terrible but their narrative inspiration is grand and I would love a parallel of that with Abyssals. <br /> <br /> Monstrance: explicitly reduce its power/influence over an Abyssal to a &quot;mere&quot; arcane link. Generally fine with how it works vis a vis Abyssal Exaltation. Not too many complaints here really but I clearly have a different interpretation over what it can do to an Abyssal than you do.<br /> <br /> Deathlords: better mechanics, more interesting fluff, etc etc what I want here is irrelevant/not worth repeating because the authors have already said they're doing pretty much what I would want for the Deathlords, so. Perfectly fine with most Abyssals being personally chosen at the point of death by a Deathlord and offered Exaltation, but intrigued by what Vance has said about independent Abyssals being more supported from the get-go.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>kindledRadial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/333352-3e-abyssals-exalted-hauntings?p=338573#post338573\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">ALSO I still want to discuss my original thread question of &quot;would tying resonance eruptions to abyssal motivation rather than an NPC be fun for people, and/or better than what we have.&quot; So if people could start relating their comments back to that question I'd greatly appreciate it.</div> </div> </div> </div>2e's nonsensical Motivations are thankfully going away and I don't think Resonance keying off of Defining Intimacies is a good idea. But really anything is better than the stupid Neverborn choke chain. With Virtues also going the way of the dodo I imagine it'll trigger off of whatever triggers the Great Curse, but we have no clue what that will be or how it'll be implemented.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-12T20:03:50-08:00","id":338642,"title":"","content":"At least Limit Break fill my WP pool, Resonance just kills my kitty :'(","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The no.1 fan of Demetheus. I also draw <a href=\"https://probably-unreliable.tumblr.com/tagged/Jenart\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted</a> things and is looking for commission works ~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","name":"Jen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar298_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-12T20:14:13-08:00","id":338647,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/333352-3e-abyssals-exalted-hauntings?p=338628#post338628\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">2e's nonsensical Motivations are thankfully going away and I don't think Resonance keying off of Defining Intimacies is a good idea. But really anything is better than the stupid Neverborn choke chain. With Virtues also going the way of the dodo I imagine it'll trigger off of whatever triggers the Great Curse, but we have no clue what that will be or how it'll be implemented.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wait when did they say the virtues were going away? I know the rest of it I hadn't heard anything about the virtue stats being pulled too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-12T20:15:04-08:00","id":338648,"title":"","content":"Korekore: obviously I don't need to tell my ST what I think but just for the record I agree with most of what korekore has here except that I would like &quot;upwelling from oblivion&quot; to be more in line with how Ignis &quot;empowers&quot; the solar exaltation. Yes they are influenced by him but he can't just yank on the solar leash and make them do what he wants. Solars <i>tend</i> to be like Sol because they get similar <i>powers</i> as him, but in Ex2 we never explored any other avenues for Oblivion powers other than &quot;killing extras.&quot; I'd like to see Oblivion being more of a thematic influence and less an overbearing overlord in Ex3, with more end games than just &quot;best murderer in Creation.&quot; Hence my idea where the &quot;blackness&quot; of the black exaltation comes from Oblivion and informs its charms, but that doesn't mean you have to take your <i>character's</i> lead from oblivion.<br /> <br /> Zelbinnean: thank you very much for sharing. Pretty much entirely on board with all your main points here. You and I <i>do</i> seem to be interpreting the canon for monstrances differently but I think we see the same problems. I also like the idea of treating it as a normal arcane link, with maybe an explicit understanding that a Deathlord always knows where you are through it (maybe skry-proof-proof?). Since I also am curious what we will get to use as triggers for the Great Curse in Ex3 I am a bit afraid to post any ideas here on how to add a carrot element to resonance but it's not a bad idea. Maybe in my version it could be that the black exaltation works through your lower soul and makes you more bestial when triggered, like a WoD vampire going crazy from hunger, but that indulging your hungers at this time gives willpower/motes?<br /> <br /> Nalak: you're getting angry because I'm telling you what <i>you </i>think and I'm getting angry because you keep telling me what <i>I</i> think. We should stop that. Here's what I <i>actually</i> want for abyssal revisions, I'd appreciate it if you posted what <i>you</i> wanted, not as a response to what I have here but simply as an expression of your hopes for Ex3:<br /> <br /> Resonance and Neverborn: no longer a tool of the Neverborn/Deathlords for making you play the evil psycho archetype. Abyssals might still be rooted in oblivion or the Neverborn but this is a thematic link and not &quot;the NPC owns my character&quot; bullshit. Resonance should still be very unpleasant for the character when triggered, as in Shards, but the triggering condition should have <i>nothing</i> to do with what a canon NPC wants from your character. Personally I like the idea of the abyssal exaltation itself being the source of resonance, but that this is not its idea of &quot;punishment&quot; so much as its way of motivating you to be all you can be. So if the Solar exaltation were like a really good personal assistant that got you everything you asked for the abyssal exaltation would be like a slightly psychotic drill sergeant barking at you to stop making excuses and do the thing. You get the same job done just as well though.<br /> <br /> Monstrances and Deathlords: I hate what they are in canon, and this thread has convinced me that scaling monstrances back to <i>just</i> arcane links would be the best thing. Let the Deathlords be scary enough on their own that just having them <i>know</i> where you are is threat enough to make you reconsider rebellion, which is only <i>if</i> you decided to make a loyalist in the first place. This should be completely optional.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1318-kindledradial","name":"kindledRadial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1318_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-12T20:18:43-08:00","id":338651,"title":"","content":"Resonance... I have mixed feelings on. On one hand, sure. It's a nice way to have something similar to, 'Reality hates your guts and it SHOWS'. But that's not what it is. It's, 'Your masters can kick you in your metaphorical nuts if you break their heavily restrictive rules'. On one hand, sure. Being bound directly to the neverborn is a HORRIBLE thing. But at the same time, you're not often. Pulling a number out of my rear end, my instinctive estimate is that there's 10, MAYBE 15 shards out there that don't have a monstrance. I haven't poked CoCD: Underworld, or MoEP: Abyssals that much. Dunno if they ever mention that. Anyway, back to resonance. I think that something as, 'DEATH DESPAIR GLOOM DOOM' as that is... OK? But it just feels like crap for crap's sake. Shoehorning you into a role (Unrepentant deathly supersoldier) for a reason I think we've all speculated on with varying degrees of rancor. I have no idea what it is, personally. The reason why I gave that a tentative, 'OK' is because it has bits and pieces of gothic lit type horror (Masque of Red Death-based resonance blight anyone?), which fit the theme of the Underworld very well. Just not abyssals.<br /> <br /> That having been said, I kind of want something like mounting penalties for operating in a place removed from the Underworld sooner than Resonance. Like, the more life-aligned a place you find yourself in the more it screws with you. Temple to TUS? &quot;IT BURNS!&quot; Wood manse? Twitching and running away. Creation? Mild unease, like mortals probably feel in the Underworld for other reasons like the general gloomy atmosphere... That can increase to pants-wetting terror when you see a necrotech beastie. I'm not talking about, 'Solar shows up, you fall down dead because hunter vs. vampire LOL'. I'm just talking about... I -guess- the idea of the, 'Revive Kills Zombie' trope if that makes any sense.<br /> <br /> Monstrances are a different story. Fundamentally, I have a weird appreciation for and hatred of them at the same time. On one hand, it DOES provide the classic, 'I have you now my pretty!' type situation. Bastila with Malak, Dorothy in the Wizard of Oz as mentioned, if you want a less torture-based but similar countdown to horrible deal. THAT is a good trope, fun to add an element of crisis. But at the same time... It vaguely feels like, 'Torture makes you evil'. Which I have mixed feelings about. I mean sure, you CAN go crazy from trauma, it's just a thing. But I don't like the idea of, 'Being tortured turns you into a baby-eating unrepentant monster'. It just feels like taking a victim and setting them up to get put through, 'Ron the Death Eater' treatment.<br /> <br /> Coupled with resonance as it exists now, I will admit. It does have a synergy between, 'Break you with the monstrance, rein you in with resonance'. But given resonance's problems, I just don't like the idea of it being able to so thoroughly screw over a player, taking them from functional hero one moment and putting them under a villain's thumb nigh-irreperably the next. Sure it would take a horrible ST to just rip any semblance of control away from your character like that? But the possibility that it could happen as part of the course of dramatic progression is a bit unsettling.<br /> <br /> Aaaaaand onto deathlords. Deathlords didn't get enough characterization. I feel like they should be their own, 'Thing' or class of entity. Painting them as uberghosts with solar charms and true immortality is stupid for a few reasons. First of all, it just... Kills how they feel mechanically. They don't feel like, 'I have deathly power over ghosts as a whole' any more than... Well, your average necromancer. Even their kill-stare is kind of weird, vaguely feeling like a necromantic spell. That having been said, given the lack of mysterious non-charm non-spell non-MA abilities as prevalent in exalted... This is one of their better points on a fluff-mechanics interaction basis to me.<br /> <br /> When playing an abyssal exalt, I have to say that I do prefer the idea of having a more meaningful connection to your liege. Before it just felt like picking a patron in D&amp;D for your cleric. Distant and kindasorta there, but more a background fluff thing that informs your general and vague ethos than it does actually influence your immediate actions or your unique capabilities. I'm not asking for the hardcoded rules of resonance. More like, 'You have a few extra tricks exclusive to serving a given liege that only work in situations where they would act similarly'. Almost 2e's yozi charms with a deathly flair and less specific restrictions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2532-blitzkitty","name":"BlitzKitty","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2532_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"72"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-12T20:18:48-08:00","id":338652,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nalak42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/333352-3e-abyssals-exalted-hauntings?p=338647#post338647\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wait when did they say the virtues were going away? I know the rest of it I hadn't heard anything about the virtue stats being pulled too.</div> </div> </div> </div>I can't remember exactly when this was first brought up but it's been confirmed for a while now.<br /> <br /> Basically the narrative notions of Virtue stuff (high Compassion = less likely to callously ignore suffering, for example) will be rolled into Intimacies, like you can have an Intimacy towards being charitable as easily as you can toward your spouse or your homeland or a particular goal. Intimacies were already a pretty good model for Conviction, i.e. &quot;things you care about in more than just a passing fond way.&quot;<br /> <br /> The mechanical implementation of Virtue channels likely will be gone since the stats will be gone. <br /> <br /> No clue what the Great Curse will be based on or implemented but I gather from the authorial criticism of the 1e/2e method that it will be much less &quot;random psychotic break from built-up stress that is poignant but only lasts one session because to make it longer would be too disruptive.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-12T20:22:55-08:00","id":338654,"title":"","content":"&quot;You tried to mind-control me? WHY IS THE WORLD SO HORRIBLE? OMG!&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2532-blitzkitty","name":"BlitzKitty","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2532_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"72"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-12T20:39:48-08:00","id":338678,"title":"","content":"Resonance: It should be possible to disengage this from ANY sort of guiding &quot;intelligence&quot; by simply saying that it is the &quot;feedback&quot; reaction that occurs when the unnatural energy of death that powers Abyssals runs up against life-affirming actions by the Deathknight. Done! <br /> <br /> As to how to implement it mechanically, it seems that a lot of objections come down to players just not wanting Bad Things to happen to their PCs, and since the entire concept is that Bad Things Happen, maybe there's just NO way to model it without pissing off the players...<br /> <br /> Monstrances: Canonically, there ARE Abyssals who don't have Monstrances, just as there are Deathlords who simply let their Exaltations fly free and exalt whoever they could find (personally, if anything, I dislike the notion that DLs can choose just *anyone*, even on the basis of their hair color!), so there's already more variety in the setting than some realize. <br /> <br /> Restricting the DLs ability to reach the Monstrance might be a good idea, however; if they're all kept in the Labyrinth, so that one has to take a lengthy trip to get to them, that might give a Deathknight some breathing room. But personally, I like the notion that a Deathknight determined to go renegade has to come up with a plan to steal his Monstrance first...then maybe he wraps it in chains and drags it around behind him to put his enemies in...<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Deathlords: With well-designed Arcanoi, from Ess 1 to 10 (and most ghosts being limited to 5), there's no reason why the Deathlords can't be dangerous, but defeatable, opponents while &quot;just&quot; being ancient, high Essence ghosts. Probably the biggest problem is that they can get pwned by anyone with Holy charms. Unless their Neverborn masters provide them with a constant defense against those. This can be tied into the Secret Weakness, which is something personal that offends the Neverborn enough that they temporarily withdraw their protection, exposing the DL to Holy attacks for the scene. Of course, you will want to give every splat some Holy powers, so as not to deprotagonize any of them...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-12T22:14:20-08:00","id":338722,"title":"","content":"Zelbinnean: I for one am tremendously pleased to be saying goodbye to statted virtues and the XP sink that goes into playing &quot;better' personalities.<br /> <br /> Blitzkitty: right now I feel like we have the worst of both worlds in terms of the Deathlord/knight dynamic: the Deathlords offer nothing in the way of personal help or guidance to their exalts but they <i>do</i> keep them on a very tight leash, popping in at the worst moments to lay down the law with a good firm press of their resonance buttons. It's like if Darth Vader raised his apprentice by throwing him alone into the swamps of Nandu, but popped in via force projection to stab him with a lightsaber whenever his apprentice considered trying to make friends with frogs. Much as I have serious concerns about a Deathlord charmset as the <i>basis</i> for the new Deathknights, I would be very happy to see these opened up to loyalists and this used as a carrot to promote that story.<br /> <br /> Hand-of-Omega: good point about the resonance, seems like we might maybe be building a consensus here that <i>if</i> we kept resonance which is still my preference then it would be best tied to the exaltation or the character or else some neutral force and not a specific NPC with an agenda. I wanna interject though because I know that no one here <i>actually </i>thinks that the ouch-factor of resonance is the problem entire with it. Obviously, resonance should suck. Maybe we should be trying to work on <i>how </i>resonance can suck in a way that is distinct from the Great Curse, since that is where we will start hearing different ideas?<br /> <br /> Question: what should resonance do in Ex3?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1318,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1318-kindledradial","user":"kindledRadial","date":". 12-13-2014, 01:29 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1318-kindledradial","name":"kindledRadial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1318_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-12T22:24:17-08:00","id":338723,"title":"","content":"I think my list of acceptable resonance eruption effects would include:<br /> <br /> non-damaging but very obvious stigmata; aura of the pariah where social actions besides intimidate fail or are heavily penalized; non-damaging scenery damage like bleeding walls, peeling paint, rotting food etc; implementation of interesting but non-lethal taboos such as &quot;can only survive on blood&quot; for a set period; temporary memory loss or memory loops similar to ghosts during a haunting; heightened emotional states either for you or for people around you; exaggerated aversion to sources of life such as Creation, children, sunlight etc.<br /> <br /> Things I would do away with:<br /> <br /> health level loss, because I saw this get used way too often in situations where it either affected nothing or got characters killed; <i>any</i> and <i>all</i> reference to resonance being activated by an NPC with their own set agenda; mortal extra auto-kills, since this <i>forced</i> players to play tragic loners instead of encouraging difficult mortal-exalt relationships that drove the story; any reference to wound penalties, for the same reasons as my first exemption.<br /> <br /> Triggers: acting out of turn with your own desires, like a ghost trying to ignore it's fetters and passions. I like to imagine the exaltation super-charging your lower soul which freaks out if you don't do what it wants, hence the resonance effects. I'll admit that this mechanic is very very similar to the existing Great Curse though, and might need more to make it distinct. Ideas?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1318,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1318-kindledradial","user":"kindledRadial","date":". 12-13-2014, 01:34 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1318-kindledradial","name":"kindledRadial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1318_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-13T05:14:43-08:00","id":338964,"title":"","content":"Yeeeeeeep. Like I said, resonance is good if you want a mystically afflicted person who's steeped in Edgar Allen Poe style horror. Barring the main thing that... To be honest? Abyssals aren't the victims of Gothic horror, they should be the ones that enact it. My ideal abyssal concept is an agent that straddles the line between, &quot;Horrific, symbolically meaningful effects.&quot; and, &quot;Cosmological wrongness.&quot; Strictly speaking, we DID get that with resonance in 2.5e but this was entirely the wrong way. In 2.5e, the horrific symbolism and cosmological wrongness made them cursed, made them sucky solars. In 3e, I personally want to see someone who <i>employs</i> Masque of the Red Death style mass-death. Not someone whose loved ones suffer from it because you decided to answer to your living name. You get the idea, they're the masters of the deathly imagery, and they draw power from the fact that they're a cosmological SNAFU.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2532,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2532-blitzkitty","user":"BlitzKitty","date":".  Typo 12-13-2014, 08:44 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2532-blitzkitty","name":"BlitzKitty","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2532_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"72"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-13T05:43:36-08:00","id":338976,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hand-of-Omega</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/333352-3e-abyssals-exalted-hauntings?p=338678#post338678\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">personally, if anything, I dislike the notion that DLs can choose just *anyone*, even on the basis of their hair color!\\</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually, it's not so simple. Yeah, they can pick some random shlub and offer him an exaltation - problem is, the exaltation can still say &quot;no, that person doesn't qualify&quot;. It has been mentioned in the abyssal book, that it's the main problem of this approach - they have to try to select viable candidates by observance only, which is a faulty method. <i>This</i> is why in lot of cases they simply let the exaltation fly and pick on its own.<br /> <br /> So, basically, yes, Deathlords get to pick and choose, but that doesn't mean all their choices are valid. We just generally don't hear about the unsuccesful attempts.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><i>The difference between fiction and reality? Fiction has to make sense.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/434-astralporing","name":"Astralporing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar434_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"296"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-13T07:23:38-08:00","id":339032,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Astralporing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/333352-3e-abyssals-exalted-hauntings?p=338976#post338976\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Actually, it's not so simple. Yeah, they can pick some random shlub and offer him an exaltation - problem is, the exaltation can still say &quot;no, that person doesn't qualify&quot;. It has been mentioned in the abyssal book, that it's the main problem of this approach - they have to try to select viable candidates by observance only, which is a faulty method. <i>This</i> is why in lot of cases they simply let the exaltation fly and pick on its own.<br /> <br /> So, basically, yes, Deathlords get to pick and choose, but that doesn't mean all their choices are valid. We just generally don't hear about the unsuccesful attempts.</div> </div> </div> </div>Part of the problem is that with Deathlord stats being what they are, I am pretty sure there is a Solar/Abyssal Charm that lets you notice if someone is a Heroic Mortal, or lets you turn a non-Heroc Mortal into one if you feel like it.<br /> <br /> The main qualifications for Solar Exaltation being: (1) human (system term of art describing a particular soul structure in 2e); (2) heroic (which is a system term of art describing &quot;how much you matter&quot;).<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-13T07:33:19-08:00","id":339037,"title":"","content":"...That, I -really- didn't like about 2e. Heroism being reduced to a binary switch, great and rare will just being an attribute you can give to people. Just kinda screws with half the setting and the importance of grand vision.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2532-blitzkitty","name":"BlitzKitty","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2532_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"72"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-13T08:04:40-08:00","id":339047,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BlitzKitty</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/333352-3e-abyssals-exalted-hauntings?p=339037#post339037\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...That, I -really- didn't like about 2e. Heroism being reduced to a binary switch, great and rare will just being an attribute you can give to people. Just kinda screws with half the setting and the importance of grand vision.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree. &quot;Heroic&quot; should be a narrative thing, not a radio button to fill in on an NPC's write-up with a Charm activation once you're bored.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-13T08:58:30-08:00","id":339115,"title":"","content":"I had a similar problem with &quot;enlightened.&quot; These were big and important ideas that <i>should</i> have meant something but instead one basically got boiled down to where you stood on the Destiny Scale of Priority and the other one was a wyld mutation. Like if they had actually made these feel like something your character worked for and earned like Samarta meditating under the tree then I would have enjoyed them, instead they became your narrative ticket to ride the exalted fun train.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1318-kindledradial","name":"kindledRadial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1318_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-13T10:19:15-08:00","id":339195,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>kindledRadial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/333352-3e-abyssals-exalted-hauntings?p=338723#post338723\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think my list of acceptable resonance eruption effects would include:<br /> <br /> non-damaging but very obvious stigmata; aura of the pariah where social actions besides intimidate fail or are heavily penalized; non-damaging scenery damage like bleeding walls, peeling paint, rotting food etc; implementation of interesting but non-lethal taboos such as &quot;can only survive on blood&quot; for a set period; temporary memory loss or memory loops similar to ghosts during a haunting; heightened emotional states either for you or for people around you; exaggerated aversion to sources of life such as Creation, children, sunlight etc</div> </div> </div> </div>These are good ideas. Mainly because they neither completely remove playa agency and shut down story (like 2e Limit) nor act as a pure punishment mechanic to direct the narrative in a narrow way (like current Resonance) nor punish you for using your divine-granted powers (like current Paradox).<br /> <br /> I see &quot;normal&quot; Limit Break, e.g. Solars and Lunars, being best described as expressions of the archetypal Greek hubris or other transcendent madness born in the heads of people who stand body-lengths above mortals in their deeds and capabilities.<br /> <br /> By contrast, Resonance seems to me like it works better as something that bleeds into the environment from the victim, rather than existing in the victim's own mind only. It taints the world with the All-Consuming All-Death that is the Abyssal's privilege to wield. Some of these suggestions open up story and plot ideas for both Abyssal PCs and NPCs, versus 2e Resonance being simply getting hit with an egg for having an individual personality or pursuing a goal in a way that plays to your strengths.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>kindledRadial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/333352-3e-abyssals-exalted-hauntings?p=338723#post338723\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Triggers: acting out of turn with your own desires, like a ghost trying to ignore it's fetters and passions. I like to imagine the exaltation super-charging your lower soul which freaks out if you don't do what it wants, hence the resonance effects. I'll admit that this mechanic is very very similar to the existing Great Curse though, and might need more to make it distinct. Ideas?</div> </div> </div> </div>I prefer not to get into the too-specific Exaltation mechanics that 2e insisted on exploring. But other than the &quot;super charging your po&quot; part I could get behind this as long as it does not require the Abyssal to be predictable or have a psyche that is mostly static (like a ghost).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rater202</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Resonance comes from neither the Death Lords, Nor the Neverborn, Nor the Abyssal's Exaltation. Rather, it is drawn from the paradox of a living-even immortal, being channeling the power of Death and perhaps Oblivion itself.<br /> <br /> If one preforms strong acts that affirm life over the dead without taking proper precautions, the resonance may build up and lash out at you. It should hurt you and you alone, or maybe cuase small plants to wilt. But that's it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Really cool ideas.<br /> <br /> Definitely can get behind the 2nd paragraph.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-13T10:28:15-08:00","id":339212,"title":"","content":"I'm gonna be honest, I was pretty happy with Abyssal Dooms from Shards. I would be cool with something in that vein.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/104-gayo","name":"Gayo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar104_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1948"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-13T18:09:57-08:00","id":339620,"title":"","content":"Gayo: It's been a while since I read shards and I can't seem to find my copy, but I remember that it did at least address my core complaint which was that it removed the Neverborn/Deathlord's ability to push the resonance bad touch button any time they liked. Since I can't find my copy could you post here what you liked about it, personally?<br /> <br /> Rater: I'm all on board for all of this so long as we get more to <i>do</i> with oblivion powers than just kill things. I'd like social charms based on negating intimacies with a sense of ennui, or super-charging them with the awareness of one's own imminent demise. I'd like a Deathknight social build who mass-produces heroic mortals by pointing at them and saying &quot;you will die <i>today</i> unless you go live your dream <i>right now</i>&quot; and they fucking do it. Or a bureaucrat who builds organizations where nothing breaks and no one ever acts out of turn because that organization is charged with the unchanging perfection of undeath. Abyssal medicine-men that can cure any disease by rendering your body inert for a week until the virus moves on, etc.. Just <i>more ideas</i> that are playable with their charmset.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1318-kindledradial","name":"kindledRadial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1318_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-13T18:44:15-08:00","id":339635,"title":"","content":"Something I would like for Resonance is for it to be standard progression. To clarify in 2nd resonance was something you rolled for whenever you did something to trigger it and you had more dice the higher your essence allowing for more resonance potential per transgression. I mean I get the narrative concept that a stronger Abyssal has more expectations from their bosses and thus transgressions could hit harder. The problem was it made it really annoying to track and felt like it punished the players for trying to get a higher essence rating. That and the bit where attempting to repent to burn away resonance could also result in more resonance just bugged me.<br /> <br /> So I don't mind if the new resonance system has it where certain offenses hit harder than others. (like you get one point for using your name and 4 for having a kid) Just I don't want it to be random so its like one time a guy has a kid but good roll means no resonance another time he responds to his name and gets max resonance.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-13T20:07:56-08:00","id":339700,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>kindledRadial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/333352-3e-abyssals-exalted-hauntings?p=339620#post339620\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Gayo: It's been a while since I read shards and I can't seem to find my copy, but I remember that it did at least address my core complaint which was that it removed the Neverborn/Deathlord's ability to push the resonance bad touch button any time they liked. Since I can't find my copy could you post here what you liked about it, personally?</div> </div> </div> </div>OK, so the Doom of the Black Exaltation kept the general incentive structure, in terms of what adds Resonance and how you get rid of it, though the costs might have been retooled a bit. But you still get Resonance for having children, going too long without killing any sentient beings, etc, you still remove it by spending time in shadowlands or adopting the trappings of the dead, and so forth. I like these things, and I think they're important for distinguishing Abyssals from Solars with a focus on death. There's nothing about the agenda to kill the world, though, they're just &quot;carrying the essence of death within you&quot;, which I find a lot more palatable than it being a chain your evil masters use to jerk you around. On reread I think it might still be a little too harsh a death spiral, given how serious the Dooms are -- the game shouldn't generally make a player feel obligated to spend three days of game time doing nothing just to chill out -- but it's a huge improvement.simply because it's about <i>you</i>.<br /> <br /> If you get to Resonance 10, you go into a Limit Break that draws on abyssal themes. As with Solar Limit Breaks, there's a related condition that causes you to gain extra Resonance. These are serious (many of them involve a compulsion to kill), but while a few are just reskinned Solar Limit Breaks, many are really thematically excellent and are a vehicle for expressing your character's nature, rather than simply blighting the world. For instance, the Doom of the Grave Blade inspires you to kill those who do not fear of death, but if they survive you feel you owe them a favour out of respect. The Doom of the Killing Saint inspires you to kill those whose suffering you cannot otherwise alleviate. The Doom of the Black Sun causes you to compulsively avoid the light of the sun. These are pretty rough given that you can't take them as &quot;partial&quot; effects and it's a nuisance to lose Resonance, but it's a <i>far</i> more compelling vision of it than<br /> <br /> In the meantime, your passive Resonance creates cool spooky effects based on how high it is. This is basically just a grab bag of neat occult effects which are mostly cosmetic but can be stunted in practical ways. Dogs howl as you approach. people think they see your shadow moving out of the corner of their eye, candles blow out in your presence, omens of death happen to occur as you pass, mirrors crack, ghostly figures seem to lurk in the fog, etc. At low resonance these seem coincidental and become more dramatic as you near the maximum, particularly when you're stressed out.<br /> <br /> (Also, you have a regular key virtue instead of a fucking broken virtue. goddamn broken virtues!)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/104-gayo","name":"Gayo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar104_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1948"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-13T20:59:44-08:00","id":339714,"title":"","content":"Nalak: Sometimes I forget exactly <i>how bad</i> the canon rules are, because my ST and I never use them. This rule never made sense to us, especially because it was <i>so easy</i> to assign a resonance cost to things on a scale of 1-5. We also usually went with whatever resonance eruption made the most sense for the story rather than rolling on a chart as I think is also canon. Just simple, common sense shit that makes this more narrative and which I'd <i>really</i> like to see become the canon standard in Ex3.<br /> <br /> Gayo: Yeah seems like I remembered more or less correctly that it was just an overall improvement. While we're on the topic though I'd <i>really</i> like to be able to play an abyssal in Ex3 who is not a sociopath about killing people. Like so much of what they are in Ex2 forces you to just get used to killing and I hate that because I personally think that is a very strong character decision to have made <i>for you</i>.<br /> <br /> I dunno, does anyone else feel that way, that abyssal's being forced to kill people whether they want to or not is too much? I'd really like to be able to play like, a daybreak occult-spec who just wants to help ghosts pass into lethe or a Midnight social who campaigns for undead rights and a more visible underworld population. Affixing &quot;and also they go nuts and kill people occasionally&quot; to that is really not something I'm into.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1318-kindledradial","name":"kindledRadial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1318_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-13T22:31:42-08:00","id":339752,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>kindledRadial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/333352-3e-abyssals-exalted-hauntings?p=339714#post339714\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Gayo: Yeah seems like I remembered more or less correctly that it was just an overall improvement. While we're on the topic though I'd <i>really</i> like to be able to play an abyssal in Ex3 who is not a sociopath about killing people. Like so much of what they are in Ex2 forces you to just get used to killing and I hate that because I personally think that is a very strong character decision to have made <i>for you</i>.<br /> <br /> I dunno, does anyone else feel that way, that abyssal's being forced to kill people whether they want to or not is too much? I'd really like to be able to play like, a daybreak occult-spec who just wants to help ghosts pass into lethe or a Midnight social who campaigns for undead rights and a more visible underworld population. Affixing &quot;and also they go nuts and kill people occasionally&quot; to that is really not something I'm into.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think Abyssals should be <i>forced</i> to kill people, but I think it's fine for them to suffer more than anyone else for <i>not</i> killing people, and for them to be more likely to kill people against their best intentions. If <i>all</i> the Dooms involved killing people that'd be bad, but I think it's appropriate that more of them do than Solar Limit Breaks, and that never killing anybody exacerbates Resonance. If you take the Doom of the Stabby Motherfucker rather than the Doom of the Runny Mascara, you're making a definite statement about the kind of person your character is and the kind of stories you want to tell about them.<br /> <br /> The thing is, okay: I've seen a Solar PC who was deathly pale, came from a shadowland, adopted the trappings of death, and campaigned for undead rights and a more visible underworld population. (She also killed people a lot, but that's an aside.) That's <i>off-type</i> for a Solar, but it's not <i>inappropriate</i>, and the character was definitely a Solar and not an Abyssal. You can be a necromancer who spends most of your time in Shadowlands and the Underworld, is deeply concerned with death and the dead, and wears soulsteel, and be a Solar. The distinction between Abyssals and Solars runs deeper than that, and part of it is that Abyssals are <i>cursed </i>in a much more ostantatious and death-themed way than Solars (whose Great Curse, by comparison, is mostly just about extremeness of temperament). This is supposed to be kind of a cool thematic thing rather than a &quot;fuck you&quot; thing, but if you're not the kind of person who thinks that the conflict between the desires of a living human and the heavy mantle of a death god is an interesting thing to play, I think Abyssals are probably not your jam. Solars <i>can </i>dress like dead people, but Abyssals <i>need</i> to, because being able to play someone who dresses like a dead person but would rather not is part of the play experience Abyssals offer that other splats don't. The killing thing is similar, though since it's more extreme it needs to be handled with more care.<br /> <br /> So I think that if you're specifically avoiding killing anybody -- which is unusual for <i>any</i> Exalted PC, let's face it -- there should be some pain associated with that. The &quot;pain&quot; should be calibrated to be playable, and you should have some latitude to decide how harsh you want it to be, but it shouldn't be purely cosmetic and trivial.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":104,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/104-gayo","user":"Gayo","date":". 12-14-2014, 01:35 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/104-gayo","name":"Gayo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar104_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1948"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-13T22:59:34-08:00","id":339764,"title":"","content":"Well the devs have stated that part of the redesign on Abyssals is so they can be more than walking murder machines. I don't recall the exact wording but they basically mentioned how the old charms had the issue of being all about murder to the extent where you couldn't really play a character who wasn't focused on slaughter.<br /> <br /> @KindledRadical Yeah the rolled resonance thing got absurd but the chart was basically just &quot;here are the types of resonance afflictions and here's what X amount of points in each does.&quot; Though the fact that you could apparently fail a resonance vent, which gave you the full vent and then added resonance to your total, is just additional absurdity. I mean I get that resonance was meant to be a punishment, but I almost question the point of giving the player the option to lose points of resonance when it seems so much like the goal was just to make the player hit ten and suck the big hit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-14T00:44:15-08:00","id":339812,"title":"","content":"...Honestly, I'd really like that. In 2e, it felt like most of their charms boiled down to, 'Like solars, except instead of being able to do things in general it can only do something deathly/facepunchy/horrible'.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2532-blitzkitty","name":"BlitzKitty","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2532_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"72"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-14T09:16:54-08:00","id":340092,"title":"","content":"Gayo: just to clarify I still think it's appropriate to provide more <i>incentives</i> for deathknights to kill people than other splats. Like being able to vent resonance by killing sentients would be appropriate and cool to me, so long as we also had other, non-violent ways of venting resonance so that playing a non-murder abyssal was not penalized as a playstyle in and of itself. What I'm really concerned with is the low-tier &quot;resonance killed your baby&quot; eruption which is an auto-kill and makes being around the abyssal in and of itself a death sentence. Like many characters could thrive on that dynamic, but some are soft souls who would see no alternative besides living a secluded life in a hermitage for the rest of their exaltation. And that's boring. Ever been to a hermitage? Boring. No offense to hermits, be there any reading this thread now. Point is, I'd like to preserve the fact that living amongst the living is harder for abyssals without their mechanics resulting in inevitable body counts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1318-kindledradial","name":"kindledRadial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1318_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-14T10:21:00-08:00","id":340116,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>kindledRadial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/333352-3e-abyssals-exalted-hauntings?p=340092#post340092\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Gayo: just to clarify I still think it's appropriate to provide more <i>incentives</i> for deathknights to kill people than other splats. Like being able to vent resonance by killing sentients would be appropriate and cool to me, so long as we also had other, non-violent ways of venting resonance so that playing a non-murder abyssal was not penalized as a playstyle in and of itself. What I'm really concerned with is the low-tier &quot;resonance killed your baby&quot; eruption which is an auto-kill and makes being around the abyssal in and of itself a death sentence. Like many characters could thrive on that dynamic, but some are soft souls who would see no alternative besides living a secluded life in a hermitage for the rest of their exaltation. And that's boring. Ever been to a hermitage? Boring. No offense to hermits, be there any reading this thread now. Point is, I'd like to preserve the fact that living amongst the living is harder for abyssals without their mechanics resulting in inevitable body counts.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I'd be happy to see the &quot;Black Miracle&quot; style of resonance eruption gone entirely. The knots they had to tie themselves into to prevent it from being used for personal benefits seem to suggest that there were problems with the concept, anyway. I think if people just <i>randomly</i> die around you for no reason because resonance that should probably be opt-in.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/104-gayo","name":"Gayo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar104_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1948"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-14T11:17:03-08:00","id":340146,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gayo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/333352-3e-abyssals-exalted-hauntings?p=340116#post340116\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah, I'd be happy to see the &quot;Black Miracle&quot; style of resonance eruption gone entirely. The knots they had to tie themselves into to prevent it from being used for personal benefits seem to suggest that there were problems with the concept, anyway. I think if people just <i>randomly</i> die around you for no reason because resonance that should probably be opt-in.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah its tricky to have something that is supposed to penalize a character also be one of their more serious weapons and more so can be charged by introducing yourself.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-14T22:09:45-08:00","id":340501,"title":"","content":"Honestly I never saw Resonance used effectively as a weapon in my games because it only ever auto-kills humans. The number of exalted in my games who have successfully leveraged mortal humans into a threat against other celestial is exactly zero. Literally the only thing that comes to mind is that you could use this in a fight against another abyssal to deprive them of a mote source in Ex2.0, because <i>mortals don't matter</i>. One of the things I kinda hope they address in Ex3, but I'm not holding my breath, even with what I do know about decisive attacks and such coming up.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1318-kindledradial","name":"kindledRadial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1318_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-14T23:11:53-08:00","id":340548,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>kindledRadial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/333352-3e-abyssals-exalted-hauntings?p=340501#post340501\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Honestly I never saw Resonance used effectively as a weapon in my games because it only ever auto-kills humans. The number of exalted in my games who have successfully leveraged mortal humans into a threat against other celestial is exactly zero. Literally the only thing that comes to mind is that you could use this in a fight against another abyssal to deprive them of a mote source in Ex2.0, because <i>mortals don't matter</i>. One of the things I kinda hope they address in Ex3, but I'm not holding my breath, even with what I do know about decisive attacks and such coming up.</div> </div> </div> </div>I can't say how effective resonance is as a weapon in exalt to exalt combat, but if you're going with the goal of mass slaughter then yeah its a good weapon. Heck one of the bigger meta threats I ever levied against my players was the threat of creating an abyssal that is aware of how to abuse the resonance system. See most mortals don't matter (they should but more often than not they don't) but people have things which are important to them. Those mortals are important. You kill the towns that make up the start of a solar's kingdom he'll feel it. Massacre the army he commands and he will have to get a new one. Unleash a blight on forest and the forest dies. Unleash the max blight rating and you create a shadowland around you for a decent sized area. Through there mortals get ripped apart and hungry ghosts can swarm the area.<br /> <br /> As you said mechanically its not the greatest weapon and I can't swear that it works too well for killing an exalt. Still from a narrative and roleplay perspective resonance can be leveled as a weapon that at least requires consideration. One of the unwritten rules in our games was you kill any abyssal that has figured out he can weaponize his name.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}